rce-index`; `offer-variant!` re-emits the reversed-row pack; `snapshot`'s `:fences` reads pack digests); adjust `stage_e_scenarios.cljc` (checks that name `:yin.k/id-counter` or body keys; row 1's \"two encodings\" assertion keeps its meaning with the reversed-row encoding; the five currently red `stage-e-rows-test` cases: `row-1-candidates-and-encodings-test`, `row-7-failure-lower-and-lost-authority-test`, `row-3-reclaim-test`, `fork-per-host-test`, `row-5-replay-divergence-test` fail only because the world supplies no source index); `stage_e_peer.cljc`, `stage_e_process_test.clj`, `stage_e_rows_test.cljc` only if needed (the Node peer build picks up the new namespaces: check the Node peer entry namespace list/regexp and update it if it names old fixtures). Acceptance (plan 7d): `stage_e_rows_test` green on JVM (slow tier with `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`), and written so it runs on Node and Dart; `stage_e_process_test` JVM-driven over `[[:jvm :jvm] [:jvm :node] [:node :jvm] [:node :node]]` with every cut a SIGKILL: you CANNOT run it fully: run the fast-lane gate `the-cross-host-handoff-across-processes-test` on the JVM pair if your sandbox allows processes and report; the orchestrator runs the Node/process matrix on shiva and jupiter. Row 10's canonical-byte agreement across hosts holds for packs (sorted rows): keep or add the assertion. All of `yin.vm.ucf.*` green after this slice (list anything red). Also land F1, F2. Portability: `.cljc` JVM/Node/Dart (no `for` over possibly long seqs, no private var access, `(assoc {} ...)`, no unary minus on floats, `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` order, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`, no EDN strings with whitespace before closers). If the plan and the code disagree, the code wins: report design defects, never silently change semantics. Verification, foreground only, JVM: `clj -M:kondo --lint <changed files>`; `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <each touched ns>`, `-i :slow` with `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`; every `yin.vm.ucf.*` namespace; `rows_test`, harness, layout unchanged. Mutants (cp backup; diff and `git diff --quiet` to verify): fence omitted from a world step; variant offered with the counter-changed encoding accepted as equal-baseline; successor published before the fence; lost-authority check skipped; a crash cut that never fires (assert each cut fires); report accepting an unfenced result; per-host fork divergence ignored. Which does your suite catch? Do not commit. Report `collab/1792500000000-engineer-7d-stage-e.report.md`: files and line counts, test counts, mutants, what you could not run, deviations, design defects, what 7e docs need to state.\n","numLines":6,"startLine":1,"totalLines":6}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KssyqS6tfni2sPEDb5xMx4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
