{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxPALbHz68pUVF8p8is4QW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-10-14 00:40 +07\n2\t# Review findings: slice 7c, composition and fencing suites over row packs\n3\t\n4\tReviewer: claude-fable-5-1 (non-author; codex wrote 7c). Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c`, branch `srvm-phase7c`, commit `05d3a25f` over `srvm-phase7` (7a, 7b merged). Method: full read of `git diff srvm-phase7..HEAD` (six test files, no production change, confirmed by `--name-only`), the brief, codex's report and mutant artifacts (`target/7c-mutants/`), `7a-report.md` (D1, D2), `7b-review.md` (F1-F3), the plan (§1.1, §3.3-3.6, slice 7c); the production seams the suites exercise (`compose.cljc` check!/holder-config-keys/driver-config, `driver.cljc` export-prepare/fence/offer/lower/step-validating, `export.cljc` prepare/encode/freeze, `rows.cljc` check-custody!/accept-grant!/with-custody/lower-task/check-install!, `rows/checkpoint.cljc`, `authority/completion.cljc`); the quick and slow lanes; 16 mutants of my own with byte-level restore. JVM only (Node/Dart by reading). Nothing in the repo edited; artifacts under `target/7c-review/` (ignored).\n5\t\n6\t## Verification I ran\n7\t\n8\t| Lane | Command | Result |\n9\t|---|---|---|\n10\t| Quick, every UCF ns | `clojure -M:test -e :slow -r 'yin\\.vm\\.ucf\\..*'` (foreground, logged) | 700 tests, 9340 assertions, 0 failures, **5 errors**, all in `yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-rows-test` (`row-1-candidates-and-encodings`, `row-7-failure-lower-and-lost-authority`, `row-3-reclaim`, `fork-per-host`, `row-5-replay-divergence`), each `The custody composition needs a source index` thrown at `compose.cljc:104` from `open!`: `stage_e_world/composition-config` supplies no `:source-index`. No other namespace fails. Matches codex exactly. |\n11\t| Slow, the six suites | `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n` the six namespaces | 2 tests, 435 assertions, 0 failures: `completion-recovery-unknown-policy-transaction-is-reconciled-once-test` and the driver's slow journal-cut case. Note: `dao.test-slow/enabled?` is `true` on the JVM unconditionally (`test_slow.cljc:17`), so `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` is a Node/Dart switch only; the JVM result is identical with or without it. |\n12\t| Lint | `clj -M:kondo --lint` the six files | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n13\t| Restore | `git diff --quiet -- src`, `git status --short -- src test` after the mutant pass | clean |\n14\t\n15\t## Item by item\n16\t\n17\t1. **F1, F2, F3 are real.** F1: `driver_test.cljc:3196-3201` maps the journal's `:yin.k/store` intents in order to `[(:yin.k/record fence) (:yin.k/address fence)]`; my R01 (the two `store-object` calls swapped) fails it and, independently, the content-store cuts test (8 failures). F2: `rows_custody_test.cljc:294-296` changes only the record's profile, keeping the honest input and output; my R10 (the record-address conjunct replaced by `contains?`) fails exactly that deftest (2 failures), so the conjunct is now isolated. F3: `compose_test.cljc:619` is `:source-index (fn [] {})`; the refusal message `\":source-index is a composition seam\"` matches `check-holder-config-keys!`.\n18\t2. **The re-based suites test what they claim.**\n19\t   - `compose_rows_test` content-store cuts (`:2514`): the cut fires on a freeze put (`some? cut-address` asserted); the expected addresses come from a deterministic re-`freeze` of the stalled export cell, so position 1 = recovery v2 address and position 2 = pack address is asserted against production, not against itself; `:after` cuts decode the stored object (version 2 naming the pack; the pack whose `rows/pack-address` is the store key and whose root the inspector answers); intents = position, acks = position − 1; no fence, no offer; the rebuilt composition stalls `:incomplete-preparation`, never re-mints, never fences, zero attaches. Cut names unchanged (positions 1/2 × before/after here; the named `store-put-*`/`body-put-*` cuts live in 7d's world).\n20\t   - Pack address as store key, root inside the baseline: asserted at `:2540-2543` and throughout (`:address` of the fence is what the authority admits as a variant, `:yin.k/root` only inside `inspect`'s answer).\n21\t   - Two admitted encodings: `variant-of` (`:429`) reverses `:yin.k/rows`; different pack address, same root, same baseline, admitted as a second variant and lowered by the winner (`row-1-…-two-encodings`). A counter change (`f/edit-task … [:slots 4] 9`, slot 4 is the task's id counter, `rows.cljc:1682`) is a different root and a conflicting baseline (`completion-recovery-requires-the-exact-origin-lease-body-and-successor` `:body` case). This is exactly 7a's `variant-equal` / `variant-other-root` fixtures (`rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc:230-232`, `grant_test` `:variant-conflict`), so 7c agrees with 7a D2 and with the code. I agree with the semantics: the root is the semantic identity of the continuation, a changed counter is a different continuation state; the plan's §1.1 row-1 line (\"id-counter variant, equal baseline\") is the stale text (F3 below).\n22\t   - No vacuous test found: every cut asserts it fired; the new source-index test asserts `pos? calls`, the refusal status and reason, no machine, no offer; the new unfenced-report test asserts the exact refusal map and an unchanged projection; the fencing lower asserts `pos?` attaches on success and `zero?` on the fail-closed case.\n23\t   - `fencing_rows_test`: lift under header with `@rs/source-index`; `lower-task` with `:exclusive`, `:protection`, `:grant` (evidence, binding, tenure, prefix); op-ids read from the pending row's slots at `write-slots`' indices (3/6/7, `rows.cljc:1170`), preserved through park → pack → lower → fenced retry, counter restored exactly; `markers` reads `[id kind & slots]` rows (layout at `rows.cljc:874`). Correct.\n24\t3. **`handoff_v2_authority_test`.** Deleted: `authority-for`, the `offer!` of a version-2 fork (`:not-offerable`) and exclusive (`:committed`), and the `report!` of a halted version-2 fork. All three exercise the authority over version-2 bytes, a path that no longer exists (7a D1). Kept, renamed: the inspector's fork/exclusive baselines and the halted result's origin, on all four engines; `a-fork-tree-refuses-a-carried-operation-id` untouched. Rows-side coverage of the deleted claims exists: `grant_test` `offers-the-authority-cannot-hold-are-refused` (`:not-offerable`, `:uninspectable` for a fork pack) and `completion_test` `a-halted-body-must-name-this-occurrence-and-lease` (`:wrong-origin`), plus the new `a-composed-authority-refuses-an-unfenced-result-report-test`. Nothing that remains lost coverage; nothing deleted was about remaining code. The ns docstring misnames the covering suite (F2).\n25\t4. **Stage E errors**: see the quick lane row; the five are the only red UCF tests and the cause is the missing `:source-index` at `open!`, 7d's.\n26\t5. **Slow deftests**: green, see the lane table.\n27\t6. **Portability read.** No `for`, no `#'`/private access across namespaces (everything used from `rows-support`, `rows-checkpoint-fixtures`, `rows`, `export`, `rows.checkpoint` is public), catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)` in the three new try sites, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)` order kept on the subprocess test, base64 only through `jing/base64->bytes` with `(vec …)` equality (driver_test), `(comp vec reverse)` on the rows vector, `(str (random-uuid))` was already in the file. Unverified on Node/Dart by instruction.\n28\t7. **Mutants**: table below.\n29\t\n30\t## Mutants (mine)\n31\t\n32\tDriver `target/7c-review/mut.py`; per-mutant diff, log and backup under `target/7c-review/mutants/`; each restore byte-compared and `git diff --quiet` on the file. Scoped to the named suites, quick tier.\n33\t\n34\t| Mutant | File | Killed? | By |\n35\t|---|---|---|---|\n36\t| R01 recovery stored after the pack | driver | yes (8) | `the-source-half-mints-fences-and-offers-before-candidacy-test` (F1), `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` |\n37\t| R02 custody stage after attach | rows | yes (41) | four zero-attach deftests of `rows_custody_test`, `row-2`, `row-7-a-successor-whose-lower-fails`, the fencing fail-closed case |\n38\t| R03a grant `:not-holder` check removed | rows | yes (24) | `every-grant-check-refuses-before-any-attachment` only |\n39\t| R03b `accept-grant!` skipped (nil state) in the compose path | rows | yes (304) | 40 deftests across compose-rows, fencing, rows-custody |\n40\t| R04 fenced lower gates `:running` | rows | yes (1) | `an-exclusive-blocked-root-under-fenced-skips-the-grant` only (as 7b F6 predicted; export/driver mask it via `extract-recovered`) |\n41\t| R05 offer carries the recovery address instead of the pack address | driver | yes (560) | 66 deftests across compose, compose-rows, driver |\n42\t| R06 store ack journaled before the put | driver | yes (6) | `serving-and-storage-have-write-ahead-brackets-test`, `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` |\n43\t| R06b test substrate: cut `:before`/`:after` meaning swapped | compose_rows_test | yes (1+1) | `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` (codex's M6 confirmed) |\n44\t| R07a compose hands the driver an empty source index | compose | yes (337) | 47 deftests incl. `the-source-index-is-read-from-the-composition-test`, the no-REPL subprocess test |\n45\t| R07b `open!`'s `check!` for `:source-index` removed | compose | **no** (0) | none: every composition in the suites supplies the index; no test pins the open-time refusal (F1) |\n46\t| R08a `:wrong-origin` never | completion | yes (13) | `a-composed-authority-refuses-an-unfenced-result-report-test`, `a-halted-body-must-name-this-occurrence-and-lease`, `the-report-verifies-its-successor` |\n47\t| R08b halted result skips the origin check | completion | yes (5) | the same first two |\n48\t| R09a fence record not journaled | driver | yes (98) | 45 deftests |\n49\t| R09b fence journaled without storing either object | driver | yes (28+26) | 31 deftests incl. both cut suites and `failed-recovery-store-does-not-attempt-the-body-store-test` |\n50\t| R10 Q3 record-address conjunct → `contains?` | rows | yes (2) | `the-install-response-is-verified-before-any-attachment` (F2) |\n51\t| R11 lift stops refusing missing trees | rows | yes (4) | `the-lift-takes-trees-from-the-composition-source-index-test`, `the-source-index-is-read-from-the-composition-test` |\n52\t| R12 inspector drops `:yin.k/root` from the baseline | rows/checkpoint | yes (4+13) | `a-conflicting-variant-is-refused`, the content-store cuts, 13 compose-rows exit/recovery tests |\n53\t\n54\tCodex's nine mutants are consistent with mine where they overlap (M1↔R01, M2↔R02, M3↔R03b, M4↔R04, M5↔R05, M6↔R06b, M7↔R07a, M8↔R08a, M9↔R10). Codex's claim that all eight requested mutants are caught holds; the one survivor here is a mutant outside the brief's list.\n55\t\n56\t## Findings\n57\t\n58\t| id | severity | file:line | finding | fix |\n59\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n60\t| F1 | low (test gap) | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc:682` | No test pins that `compose/open!` refuses a config without a function `:source-index` (R07b: removing the `check!` at `compose.cljc:188` passes compose-test and compose-rows-test). The refusal is exercised only by the red Stage E suite, so once 7d supplies the index nothing will guard it. | Add one case beside `a-journal-substrate-is-checked-at-open-test`: `(is (thrown-with-msg? … #\"source index\" (compose/open! (dissoc cfg :source-index))))` for both modes, and one with `:source-index {}` (not a fn). Six lines; can land with 7d or as a follow-up. |\n61\t| F2 | info | `test/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_authority_test.cljc:3` | The ns docstring says the authority paths \"are covered by rows-custody-test\"; that suite covers lift/lower custody, not the authority. The rows-side coverage of the deleted assertions is `authority/grant_test` (`:not-offerable`, `:uninspectable`), `authority/completion_test` (`:wrong-origin`) and compose-rows' new unfenced-report test. | Name those suites in the docstring. |\n62\t| F3 | info (plan amendment, 7d/7e) | `collab/phase7-plan.md` §1.1 row `[:row-1]` | The plan still says a re-emitted id-counter variant has \"a new root id and new pack; equal baseline\". With `:yin.k/root` in the baseline (§3.3, 7a) that variant is `:variant-conflict`; the only equal-baseline encoding is the same root in another row order, which 7a's fixtures, 7c's `variant-of` and the ledger all agree on. Codex reports this as deviation 2 but lists \"no design mismatch\"; it is 7a D2, unchanged. 7d's `offer-variant!` and `stage_e_scenarios` row-1 check must use the reversed-row encoding, and 7e amends the plan/continuation text. Also inherited from 7a D2: `rows/decode` accepts unsorted packs, which is what makes the second encoding admissible at all; \"one root, one pack\" is a property of `emit`, not of readers. Owner/Architect to confirm that stays so. | 7d: reversed rows for row-1's second encoding. 7e: amend §1.1 row-1 and note the decode stance. |\n63\t| F4 | info | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_rows_test.cljc:2541` | The position-2 `:after` check compares the stored wire's `:yin.k/root` with `inspect`'s `:yin.k/root`, which `inspect-pack` copies from the same wire (`rows/checkpoint.cljc:80`); the assertion's real content is that `inspect` accepts the pack. Harmless. | Optional: compare with `(:root frozen)` instead, which ties the stored pack's root to the frozen record. |\n64\t| F5 | info | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc:1118` | The source-index test can assert only `:export-refused`, not the lift's `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete` detail, because the driver's `unsatisfied` keeps `status/reason/kind/path` only. R11 (missing trees not refused) is still killed because the holder then reaches `:lifted`. | None required. |\n65\t\n66\tNo production code changed in 7c and none of my mutants found a production defect. The owner's rulings hold in the tests as written: the composition's source index is the only route for trees (R07a, R11), A names code, pack address is storage and the root is semantic (R12), no version dispatch or shim appeared, lease/epoch/holder stay out of packs (7a grammar, unchanged), `yin.repl` untouched and the no-REPL subprocess test green on the semantic-register receiver, the de Bruijn kernels untouched.\n67\t\n68\tVERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE (into the integration branch `srvm-phase7`). F1 is a six-line test addition, non-blocking; F3 is a 7d/7e note, not a 7c defect.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e817baf-a368-4767-b2d4-2b25a4b937e7","uuid":"49e7e2da-2579-4050-a4a0-8afdb235840e","timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:46:10.753Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/collab/7c-review.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 00:40 +07\n# Review findings: slice 7c, composition and fencing suites over row packs\n\nReviewer: claude-fable-5-1 (non-author; codex wrote 7c). Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7c`, branch `srvm-phase7c`, commit `05d3a25f` over `srvm-phase7` (7a, 7b merged). Method: full read of `git diff srvm-phase7..HEAD` (six test files, no production change, confirmed by `--name-only`), the brief, codex's report and mutant artifacts (`target/7c-mutants/`), `7a-report.md` (D1, D2), `7b-review.md` (F1-F3), the plan (§1.1, §3.3-3.6, slice 7c); the production seams the suites exercise (`compose.cljc` check!/holder-config-keys/driver-config, `driver.cljc` export-prepare/fence/offer/lower/step-validating, `export.cljc` prepare/encode/freeze, `rows.cljc` check-custody!/accept-grant!/with-custody/lower-task/check-install!, `rows/checkpoint.cljc`, `authority/completion.cljc`); the quick and slow lanes; 16 mutants of my own with byte-level restore. JVM only (Node/Dart by reading). Nothing in the repo edited; artifacts under `target/7c-review/` (ignored).\n\n## Verification I ran\n\n| Lane | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Quick, every UCF ns | `clojure -M:test -e :slow -r 'yin\\.vm\\.ucf\\..*'` (foreground, logged) | 700 tests, 9340 assertions, 0 failures, **5 errors**, all in `yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-rows-test` (`row-1-candidates-and-encodings`, `row-7-failure-lower-and-lost-authority`, `row-3-reclaim`, `fork-per-host`, `row-5-replay-divergence`), each `The custody composition needs a source index` thrown at `compose.cljc:104` from `open!`: `stage_e_world/composition-config` supplies no `:source-index`. No other namespace fails. Matches codex exactly. |\n| Slow, the six suites | `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n` the six namespaces | 2 tests, 435 assertions, 0 failures: `completion-recovery-unknown-policy-transaction-is-reconciled-once-test` and the driver's slow journal-cut case. Note: `dao.test-slow/enabled?` is `true` on the JVM unconditionally (`test_slow.cljc:17`), so `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` is a Node/Dart switch only; the JVM result is identical with or without it. |\n| Lint | `clj -M:kondo --lint` the six files | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| Restore | `git diff --quiet -- src`, `git status --short -- src test` after the mutant pass | clean |\n\n## Item by item\n\n1. **F1, F2, F3 are real.** F1: `driver_test.cljc:3196-3201` maps the journal's `:yin.k/store` intents in order to `[(:yin.k/record fence) (:yin.k/address fence)]`; my R01 (the two `store-object` calls swapped) fails it and, independently, the content-store cuts test (8 failures). F2: `rows_custody_test.cljc:294-296` changes only the record's profile, keeping the honest input and output; my R10 (the record-address conjunct replaced by `contains?`) fails exactly that deftest (2 failures), so the conjunct is now isolated. F3: `compose_test.cljc:619` is `:source-index (fn [] {})`; the refusal message `\":source-index is a composition seam\"` matches `check-holder-config-keys!`.\n2. **The re-based suites test what they claim.**\n   - `compose_rows_test` content-store cuts (`:2514`): the cut fires on a freeze put (`some? cut-address` asserted); the expected addresses come from a deterministic re-`freeze` of the stalled export cell, so position 1 = recovery v2 address and position 2 = pack address is asserted against production, not against itself; `:after` cuts decode the stored object (version 2 naming the pack; the pack whose `rows/pack-address` is the store key and whose root the inspector answers); intents = position, acks = position − 1; no fence, no offer; the rebuilt composition stalls `:incomplete-preparation`, never re-mints, never fences, zero attaches. Cut names unchanged (positions 1/2 × before/after here; the named `store-put-*`/`body-put-*` cuts live in 7d's world).\n   - Pack address as store key, root inside the baseline: asserted at `:2540-2543` and throughout (`:address` of the fence is what the authority admits as a variant, `:yin.k/root` only inside `inspect`'s answer).\n   - Two admitted encodings: `variant-of` (`:429`) reverses `:yin.k/rows`; different pack address, same root, same baseline, admitted as a second variant and lowered by the winner (`row-1-…-two-encodings`). A counter change (`f/edit-task … [:slots 4] 9`, slot 4 is the task's id counter, `rows.cljc:1682`) is a different root and a conflicting baseline (`completion-recovery-requires-the-exact-origin-lease-body-and-successor` `:body` case). This is exactly 7a's `variant-equal` / `variant-other-root` fixtures (`rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc:230-232`, `grant_test` `:variant-conflict`), so 7c agrees with 7a D2 and with the code. I agree with the semantics: the root is the semantic identity of the continuation, a changed counter is a different continuation state; the plan's §1.1 row-1 line (\"id-counter variant, equal baseline\") is the stale text (F3 below).\n   - No vacuous test found: every cut asserts it fired; the new source-index test asserts `pos? calls`, the refusal status and reason, no machine, no offer; the new unfenced-report test asserts the exact refusal map and an unchanged projection; the fencing lower asserts `pos?` attaches on success and `zero?` on the fail-closed case.\n   - `fencing_rows_test`: lift under header with `@rs/source-index`; `lower-task` with `:exclusive`, `:protection`, `:grant` (evidence, binding, tenure, prefix); op-ids read from the pending row's slots at `write-slots`' indices (3/6/7, `rows.cljc:1170`), preserved through park → pack → lower → fenced retry, counter restored exactly; `markers` reads `[id kind & slots]` rows (layout at `rows.cljc:874`). Correct.\n3. **`handoff_v2_authority_test`.** Deleted: `authority-for`, the `offer!` of a version-2 fork (`:not-offerable`) and exclusive (`:committed`), and the `report!` of a halted version-2 fork. All three exercise the authority over version-2 bytes, a path that no longer exists (7a D1). Kept, renamed: the inspector's fork/exclusive baselines and the halted result's origin, on all four engines; `a-fork-tree-refuses-a-carried-operation-id` untouched. Rows-side coverage of the deleted claims exists: `grant_test` `offers-the-authority-cannot-hold-are-refused` (`:not-offerable`, `:uninspectable` for a fork pack) and `completion_test` `a-halted-body-must-name-this-occurrence-and-lease` (`:wrong-origin`), plus the new `a-composed-authority-refuses-an-unfenced-result-report-test`. Nothing that remains lost coverage; nothing deleted was about remaining code. The ns docstring misnames the covering suite (F2).\n4. **Stage E errors**: see the quick lane row; the five are the only red UCF tests and the cause is the missing `:source-index` at `open!`, 7d's.\n5. **Slow deftests**: green, see the lane table.\n6. **Portability read.** No `for`, no `#'`/private access across namespaces (everything used from `rows-support`, `rows-checkpoint-fixtures`, `rows`, `export`, `rows.checkpoint` is public), catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)` in the three new try sites, `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)` order kept on the subprocess test, base64 only through `jing/base64->bytes` with `(vec …)` equality (driver_test), `(comp vec reverse)` on the rows vector, `(str (random-uuid))` was already in the file. Unverified on Node/Dart by instruction.\n7. **Mutants**: table below.\n\n## Mutants (mine)\n\nDriver `target/7c-review/mut.py`; per-mutant diff, log and backup under `target/7c-review/mutants/`; each restore byte-compared and `git diff --quiet` on the file. Scoped to the named suites, quick tier.\n\n| Mutant | File | Killed? | By |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R01 recovery stored after the pack | driver | yes (8) | `the-source-half-mints-fences-and-offers-before-candidacy-test` (F1), `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` |\n| R02 custody stage after attach | rows | yes (41) | four zero-attach deftests of `rows_custody_test`, `row-2`, `row-7-a-successor-whose-lower-fails`, the fencing fail-closed case |\n| R03a grant `:not-holder` check removed | rows | yes (24) | `every-grant-check-refuses-before-any-attachment` only |\n| R03b `accept-grant!` skipped (nil state) in the compose path | rows | yes (304) | 40 deftests across compose-rows, fencing, rows-custody |\n| R04 fenced lower gates `:running` | rows | yes (1) | `an-exclusive-blocked-root-under-fenced-skips-the-grant` only (as 7b F6 predicted; export/driver mask it via `extract-recovered`) |\n| R05 offer carries the recovery address instead of the pack address | driver | yes (560) | 66 deftests across compose, compose-rows, driver |\n| R06 store ack journaled before the put | driver | yes (6) | `serving-and-storage-have-write-ahead-brackets-test`, `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` |\n| R06b test substrate: cut `:before`/`:after` meaning swapped | compose_rows_test | yes (1+1) | `the-wired-compositions-content-store-cuts-test` (codex's M6 confirmed) |\n| R07a compose hands the driver an empty source index | compose | yes (337) | 47 deftests incl. `the-source-index-is-read-from-the-composition-test`, the no-REPL subprocess test |\n| R07b `open!`'s `check!` for `:source-index` removed | compose | **no** (0) | none: every composition in the suites supplies the index; no test pins the open-time refusal (F1) |\n| R08a `:wrong-origin` never | completion | yes (13) | `a-composed-authority-refuses-an-unfenced-result-report-test`, `a-halted-body-must-name-this-occurrence-and-lease`, `the-report-verifies-its-successor` |\n| R08b halted result skips the origin check | completion | yes (5) | the same first two |\n| R09a fence record not journaled | driver | yes (98) | 45 deftests |\n| R09b fence journaled without storing either object | driver | yes (28+26) | 31 deftests incl. both cut suites and `failed-recovery-store-does-not-attempt-the-body-store-test` |\n| R10 Q3 record-address conjunct → `contains?` | rows | yes (2) | `the-install-response-is-verified-before-any-attachment` (F2) |\n| R11 lift stops refusing missing trees | rows | yes (4) | `the-lift-takes-trees-from-the-composition-source-index-test`, `the-source-index-is-read-from-the-composition-test` |\n| R12 inspector drops `:yin.k/root` from the baseline | rows/checkpoint | yes (4+13) | `a-conflicting-variant-is-refused`, the content-store cuts, 13 compose-rows exit/recovery tests |\n\nCodex's nine mutants are consistent with mine where they overlap (M1↔R01, M2↔R02, M3↔R03b, M4↔R04, M5↔R05, M6↔R06b, M7↔R07a, M8↔R08a, M9↔R10). Codex's claim that all eight requested mutants are caught holds; the one survivor here is a mutant outside the brief's list.\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | severity | file:line | finding | fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | low (test gap) | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc:682` | No test pins that `compose/open!` refuses a config without a function `:source-index` (R07b: removing the `check!` at `compose.cljc:188` passes compose-test and compose-rows-test). The refusal is exercised only by the red Stage E suite, so once 7d supplies the index nothing will guard it. | Add one case beside `a-journal-substrate-is-checked-at-open-test`: `(is (thrown-with-msg? … #\"source index\" (compose/open! (dissoc cfg :source-index))))` for both modes, and one with `:source-index {}` (not a fn). Six lines; can land with 7d or as a follow-up. |\n| F2 | info | `test/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_authority_test.cljc:3` | The ns docstring says the authority paths \"are covered by rows-custody-test\"; that suite covers lift/lower custody, not the authority. The rows-side coverage of the deleted assertions is `authority/grant_test` (`:not-offerable`, `:uninspectable`), `authority/completion_test` (`:wrong-origin`) and compose-rows' new unfenced-report test. | Name those suites in the docstring. |\n| F3 | info (plan amendment, 7d/7e) | `collab/phase7-plan.md` §1.1 row `[:row-1]` | The plan still says a re-emitted id-counter variant has \"a new root id and new pack; equal baseline\". With `:yin.k/root` in the baseline (§3.3, 7a) that variant is `:variant-conflict`; the only equal-baseline encoding is the same root in another row order, which 7a's fixtures, 7c's `variant-of` and the ledger all agree on. Codex reports this as deviation 2 but lists \"no design mismatch\"; it is 7a D2, unchanged. 7d's `offer-variant!` and `stage_e_scenarios` row-1 check must use the reversed-row encoding, and 7e amends the plan/continuation text. Also inherited from 7a D2: `rows/decode` accepts unsorted packs, which is what makes the second encoding admissible at all; \"one root, one pack\" is a property of `emit`, not of readers. Owner/Architect to confirm that stays so. | 7d: reversed rows for row-1's second encoding. 7e: amend §1.1 row-1 and note the decode stance. |\n| F4 | info | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_rows_test.cljc:2541` | The position-2 `:after` check compares the stored wire's `:yin.k/root` with `inspect`'s `:yin.k/root`, which `inspect-pack` copies from the same wire (`rows/checkpoint.cljc:80`); the assertion's real content is that `inspect` accepts the pack. Harmless. | Optional: compare with `(:root frozen)` instead, which ties the stored pack's root to the frozen record. |\n| F5 | info | `test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc:1118` | The source-index test can assert only `:export-refused`, not the lift's `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete` detail, because the driver's `unsatisfied` keeps `status/reason/kind/path` only. R11 (missing trees not refused) is still killed because the holder then reaches `:lifted`. | None required. |\n\nNo production code changed in 7c and none of my mutants found a production defect. The owner's rulings hold in the tests as written: the composition's source index is the only route for trees (R07a, R11), A names code, pack address is storage and the root is semantic (R12), no version dispatch or shim appeared, lease/epoch/holder stay out of packs (7a grammar, unchanged), `yin.repl` untouched and the no-REPL subprocess test green on the semantic-register receiver, the de Bruijn kernels untouched.\n\nVERDICT: READY_TO_MERGE (into the integration branch `srvm-phase7`). F1 is a six-line test addition, non-blocking; F3 is a 7d/7e note, not a 7c defect.\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RxPALbHz68pUVF8p8is4QW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
