{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P4VgMewCPUZ6xoWvvqwree","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-world\n2\t  \"M-next stage E: the world one life of a crash/partition scenario runs\n3\t   in, driven only through `yin.vm.ucf.compose` (linker-dht 14.2.4,\n4\t   UCF 7.11.1 clause 10 and the composition halves of clauses 3 and 8).\n5\t\n6\t   A scenario is a sequence of lives over one root directory.  Every\n7\t   piece of state a later life may read lives on durable file media\n8\t   under that root -- the authority's ledger (a dao.stream.journal.file\n9\t   backend), every holder's progress and reply journal\n10\t   (`compose/file-journals`), the content store (a dao.jing.file\n11\t   content file, the node's carrier for bodies and code) and the side\n12\t   log of at-least-once external IO -- so a life is a fresh runtime:\n13\t   nothing in memory crosses from one life to the next.  The program\n14\t   and source streams are outside custody; each life rebuilds its own\n15\t   instance of them under their fixed identities from the life's spec,\n16\t   the way a receiver attaches a stream by its carried descriptor.\n17\t\n18\t   A life is plain data (`run-life`'s spec) and so is everything it\n19\t   reports, so the same life runs in this process (the isolated-runtime\n20\t   mode every lane has, Dart's only form) or inside a separate operating\n21\t   system process (`yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer`, the JVM and Node process\n22\t   transport) and its report is compared as data either way.\n23\t\n24\t   Kills.  Every durable medium is wrapped mortal: a named cut (the\n25\t   `cuts` table) fires at one exact boundary -- before or after a given\n26\t   journal frame, before or after a given content-store put, or after a\n27\t   composition tick whose state matches -- and from then on the life is\n28\t   dead.  Inside a peer process the cut prints its event and blocks\n29\t   until the parent destroys the process (SIGKILL); in this process it\n30\t   marks every medium dead (no further durable write happens) and\n31\t   unwinds, and the runner releases the locks the dead runtime held --\n32\t   the only thing an operating system does for a killed process.\"\n33\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n34\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n35\t            [dao.jing.file :as jing-file]\n36\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n37\t            [dao.stream.journal :as journal]\n38\t            [dao.stream.journal.file :as file-journal]\n39\t            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n40\t            #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n41\t                       [\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]]\n42\t                :clj [[clojure.java.io :as io]])\n43\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n44\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n45\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n46\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.admission :as admission]\n47\t            [yin.vm.ucf.compose :as compose]\n48\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]\n49\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n50\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint :as checkpoint]))\n51\t\n52\t\n53\t;; =============================================================================\n54\t;; Plain data\n55\t;; =============================================================================\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t(defn- host-bytes?\n59\t  [x]\n60\t  #?(:clj (bytes? x)\n61\t     :cljs (instance? js/Uint8Array x)\n62\t     :cljd (instance? typed/Uint8List x)))\n63\t\n64\t\n65\t(defn ->data\n66\t  \"`x` as plain data every host prints and reads back the same: maps,\n67\t   vectors, sets, scalars.  Host bytes become their blake3 digest\n68\t   ({::bytes hex}), so two byte strings compare equal exactly when their\n69\t   bytes are; anything else that is not data (a handle, a function, a\n70\t   machine) becomes {::opaque true}.\"\n71\t  [x]\n72\t  (cond\n73\t    (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)\n74\t        (number? x) (uuid? x))\n75\t    x\n76\t\n77\t    (host-bytes? x) {::bytes (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 x)}\n78\t    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(->data k) (->data v)])) x)\n79\t    (vector? x) (mapv ->data x)\n80\t    (set? x) (into #{} (map ->data) x)\n81\t    (sequential? x) (mapv ->data x)\n82\t    :else {::opaque true}))\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t(defn digest-of\n86\t  \"The digest form ->data gives host bytes `bs`.\"\n87\t  [bs]\n88\t  {::bytes (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 bs)})\n89\t\n90\t\n91\t;; =============================================================================\n92\t;; Scratch roots\n93\t;; =============================================================================\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t(defn temp-root\n97\t  \"A fresh scratch root under target/.\"\n98\t  []\n99\t  (str \"target/stage-e-\" (random-uuid)))\n100\t\n101\t\n102\t(defn cleanup-root!\n103\t  [dir]\n104\t  #?(:cljd (try (.deleteSync (dart-io/Directory. dir) .recursive true)\n105\t                (catch Object _ nil))\n106\t     :clj (letfn [(delete-recursively!\n107\t                    [f]\n108\t                    (when (.isDirectory f)\n109\t                      (doseq [child (.listFiles f)]\n110\t                        (delete-recursively! child)))\n111\t                    (.delete f))]\n112\t            (delete-recursively! (io/file dir)))\n113\t     :cljs (try (.rmSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true :force true})\n114\t                (catch :default _ nil))))\n115\t\n116\t\n117\t(defn- ensure-dir!\n118\t  [dir]\n119\t  #?(:cljd (let [d (dart-io/Directory. dir)]\n120\t             (when-not (.existsSync d) (.createSync d .recursive true)))\n121\t     :clj (.mkdirs (io/file dir))\n122\t     :cljs (.mkdirSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true})))\n123\t\n124\t\n125\t(defn paths\n126\t  \"The durable media of the world over `root`.\"\n127\t  [root]\n128\t  {:authority (str root \"/authority\")\n129\t   :journals (str root \"/journals\")\n130\t   :store (str root \"/store.jing\")\n131\t   :side (str root \"/side\")})\n132\t\n133\t\n134\t(defn destroy-authority!\n135\t  \"Permanently lose the authority's state under `root`: its content file\n136\t   is overwritten with bytes that are no content log, the way a lost\n137\t   disk leaves it.  No reopen can recover a ledger from it.\"\n138\t  [root]\n139\t  (let [path (str (:authority (paths root)) \"/\" file-journal/content-name)]\n140\t    #?(:cljd (.writeAsStringSync (dart-io/File. path) \"lost authority state\")\n141\t       :clj (spit path \"lost authority state\")\n142\t       :cljs (.writeFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path \"lost authority state\"))))\n143\t\n144\t\n145\t;; =============================================================================\n146\t;; The life context: events, counters, the cut and the kill\n147\t;; =============================================================================\n148\t\n149\t\n150\t(defn context\n151\t  \"A life's context.  `emit!` takes each event map as it happens (a peer\n152\t   prints it at once); `at-cut` is called when the life's cut fires: a\n153\t   peer's never returns -- the parent kills the process inside it -- and\n154\t   the in-process runner's returns so the life can unwind dead.\"\n155\t  [{:keys [cut fail emit! at-cut]}]\n156\t  {:cut cut\n157\t   :fail fail\n158\t   :failed (atom nil)\n159\t   :emit! (or emit! (fn [_]))\n160\t   :at-cut (or at-cut (fn []))\n161\t   :dead (atom false)\n162\t   :fired (atom nil)\n163\t   :hits (atom {})\n164\t   :attaches (atom 0)\n165\t   :observes (atom 0)\n166\t   :opened (atom [])})\n167\t\n168\t\n169\t(defn killed?\n170\t  [e]\n171\t  (true? (::killed (ex-data e))))\n172\t\n173\t\n174\t(defn- dead-throw!\n175\t  []\n176\t  (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a dead runtime wrote nothing\" {::killed true})))\n177\t\n178\t\n179\t(defn- fire!\n180\t  [ctx at]\n181\t  (reset! (:fired ctx) at)\n182\t  (reset! (:dead ctx) true)\n183\t  ((:emit! ctx) {:event :cut :cut (:cut ctx) :at at})\n184\t  ((:at-cut ctx))\n185\t  (throw (ex-info \"stage E: killed at a cut\" {::killed true :cut (:cut ctx)})))\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t;; =============================================================================\n189\t;; The named cuts\n190\t;; =============================================================================\n191\t\n192\t\n193\t(defn- record-is\n194\t  [journal-kind action]\n195\t  (fn [r]\n196\t    (and (= journal-kind (:yin.k/journal r))\n197\t         (or (nil? action) (= action (:yin.k/action r))))))\n198\t\n199\t\n200\t(defn- projection-of\n201\t  [c]\n202\t  (when-some [a (:authority c)]\n203\t    (authority/projection a)))\n204\t\n205\t\n206\t(defn- journal-records-of\n207\t  \"Holder `h`'s whole progress journal, read through a fresh open of its\n208\t   backend (the restart's view).\"\n209\t  [c h]\n210\t  (let [backend (get-in c [:progress h :backend])\n211\t        j (if (some? backend)\n212\t            (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! backend nil))\n213\t            (compose/journal-of c h))]\n214\t    (if (nil? j)\n215\t      []\n216\t      (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor j :dao.stream/oldest))\n217\t             records []]\n218\t        (let [answer (stream/next j cursor)]\n219\t          (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n220\t            (recur (:dao.stream/cursor answer) (conj records (:dao.stream/value answer)))\n221\t            records))))))\n222\t\n223\t\n224\t(defn- holder-records-match?\n225\t  [c h pred]\n226\t  (boolean (some pred (journal-records-of c h))))\n227\t\n228\t\n229\t(defn- exit-occurrence\n230\t  [c h]\n231\t  (get-in c [:holders h :exit :occurrence]))\n232\t\n233\t\n234\t(defn- read-values\n235\t  [h]\n236\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n237\t         values []]\n238\t    (let [r (stream/next h cursor)]\n239\t      (if (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)) (< (count values) 1000))\n240\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj values (:dao.stream/value r)))\n241\t        values))))\n242\t\n243\t\n244\t(defn inbound-of\n245\t  \"The requests of `kind` (every request when nil) that reached holder\n246\t   `h`'s inbound in this life, in stream order.\"\n247\t  [c h kind]\n248\t  (if-some [inbound (get-in c [:inbounds h])]\n249\t    (filterv #(or (nil? kind) (= kind (:yin.k/request %))) (read-values inbound))\n250\t    []))\n251\t\n252\t\n253\t(defn- admission-commit?\n254\t  \"Whether ledger record `r` is the transaction that commits an admitted\n255\t   effect: one of its datoms is the :yin.k/admitted custody fact.\"\n256\t  [r]\n257\t  (boolean (some (fn [d]\n258\t                   (and (sequential? d)\n259\t                        (= :yin.k/custody (nth d 1 nil))\n260\t                        (= :yin.k/admitted (nth d 2 nil))))\n261\t                 (get-in r [:dao.space/transaction :datoms]))))\n262\t\n263\t\n264\t(def cuts\n265\t  \"Every named cut a scenario may ask for: where it fires and when.\n266\t   :site is a journal ([:progress h] or [:reply h]), :authority, :store\n267\t   or :tick; :when is :before or :after the matched write (a tick cut\n268\t   fires after the tick whose composition matches); :match is a\n269\t   predicate over the decoded journal record, the put ({:address a}) or\n270\t   the composition; :nth counts matches (default 1).\"\n271\t  {;; ---- row 7: completion\n272\t   :row7/after-successor-append\n273\t   {:site :tick\n274\t    :match (fn [c]\n275\t             (let [s (exit-occurrence c \"h1\")]\n276\t               (and (some? s)\n277\t                    (holder-records-match?\n278\t                      c \"h1\" #(and ((record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/offer) %)\n279\t                                   (= s (:yin.k/occurrence %)))))))}\n280\t   :row7/after-resumed-report\n281\t   {:site :tick\n282\t    :match (fn [c]\n283\t             (let [l (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :lease])]\n284\t               (and (some? l)\n285\t                    (some? (get-in (projection-of c) [:leases l :yin.k/result])))))}\n286\t   :row7/after-release-append\n287\t   {:site :tick\n288\t    :match (fn [c]\n289\t             (holder-records-match?\n290\t               c \"h1\" #(and ((record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/release) %)\n291\t                            (= :dao.stream/ok (:yin.k/append %)))))}\n292\t   :row7/after-closure\n293\t   {:site :tick\n294\t    :match (fn [c]\n295\t             (let [o (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :occurrence])]\n296\t               (and (some? o)\n297\t                    (some? (get-in (projection-of c) [:occurrences o :yin.k/closed])))))}\n298\t   :row7/while-running\n299\t   {:site :tick\n300\t    :match (fn [c] (= :running (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :phase])))}\n301\t\n302\t   ;; ---- row 4 and clause 8: around the atomic effect commitment (the\n303\t   ;; ledger transaction that records the admitted effect)\n304\t   :row4/before-commit\n305\t   {:site :authority :when :before :match admission-commit?}\n306\t   :row4/after-commit\n307\t   {:site :authority :when :after :match admission-commit?}\n308\t   :row4/before-result-append\n309\t   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :before\n310\t    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/admit (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n311\t   :row4/admit-uncarried\n312\t   {:site :tick\n313\t    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/admit)))}\n314\t\n315\t   ;; ---- row 5: the input record\n316\t   :row5/input-uncarried\n317\t   {:site :tick\n318\t    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/input)))}\n319\t   :row5/input-carried\n320\t   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :after\n321\t    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/input (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n322\t\n323\t   ;; ---- row 2 and the D14 journal brackets: the export's phases\n324\t   :export/after-minted\n325\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/minted nil)}\n326\t   :export/after-serve-intent\n327\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/serve)}\n328\t   :export/after-serve-ack\n329\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/serve)}\n330\t   :export/after-store-intent\n331\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/store)}\n332\t   :export/store-put-before\n333\t   {:site :store :when :before :match (fn [_] true)}\n334\t   :export/store-put-after\n335\t   {:site :store :when :after :match (fn [_] true)}\n336\t   :export/after-store-ack\n337\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/store)}\n338\t   :export/before-fenced\n339\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/fenced nil)}\n340\t   :export/after-fenced\n341\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/fenced nil)}\n342\t   :export/after-offer-intent\n343\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/offer)}\n344\t   :export/after-offer-attempt\n345\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/offer)}\n346\t   :export/after-offer-ack\n347\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/offer)}\n348\t\n349\t   ;; ---- the inbox retention machine (D15a) and the grant bracket\n350\t   :inbox/before-retention\n351\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/inbox nil)}\n352\t   :inbox/after-retention\n353\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/inbox nil)}\n354\t   :journal/before-proposal-attempt\n355\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/proposal)}\n356\t   :journal/after-proposal-intent\n357\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/proposal)}\n358\t   :journal/after-grant-ack\n359\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/grant)}\n360\t   :journal/after-resumed-intent\n361\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/resumed)}\n362\t   :journal/after-release-intent\n363\t   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/release)}\n364\t\n365\t   ;; ---- clause 8: after the first commit's reply stands\n366\t   :clause8/committed\n367\t   {:site :tick\n368\t    :match (fn [c]\n369\t             (some #(and (= :yin.k/admit (:yin.k/reply %))\n370\t                         (= :committed (get-in % [:yin.k/answer :yin.k/admission])))\n371\t                   (if-some [j (get-in c [:reply-journals \"h1\" :journal])]\n372\t                     (read-values j)\n373\t                     [])))}\n374\t\n375\t   ;; ---- row 6: a lost reply (the process dies before the front's\n376\t   ;; append of the proposal's reply)\n377\t   :row6/proposal-reply-lost\n378\t   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :before\n379\t    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/proposal (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n380\t\n381\t   ;; ---- the freeze's second stored object (the body)\n382\t   :export/body-put-before\n383\t   {:site :store :when :before :match (fn [_] true) :nth 2}\n384\t   :export/body-put-after\n385\t   {:site :store :when :after :match (fn [_] true) :nth 2}\n386\t\n387\t   ;; ---- clause 3: between assign and discharge\n388\t   :seq/after-assign\n389\t   {:site :tick\n390\t    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/admit)))}})\n391\t\n392\t\n393\t(defn- cut-spec\n394\t  [ctx]\n395\t  (when-some [k (:cut ctx)]\n396\t    (or (get cuts k)\n397\t        (throw (ex-info \"stage E: unknown cut\" {:cut k})))))\n398\t\n399\t\n400\t(defn- hit!\n401\t  \"Whether the life's cut matches this write at `site` (counted against\n402\t   :nth), answering :before, :after or nil.\"\n403\t  [ctx site subject]\n404\t  (let [spec (cut-spec ctx)]\n405\t    (when (and (some? spec)\n406\t               (nil? @(:fired ctx))\n407\t               (= site (:site spec))\n408\t               ((:match spec) subject))\n409\t      (let [n (get (swap! (:hits ctx) update site (fnil inc 0)) site)]\n410\t        (when (= n (or (:nth spec) 1))\n411\t          (or (:when spec) :after))))))\n412\t\n413\t\n414\t;; =============================================================================\n415\t;; Mortal media\n416\t;; =============================================================================\n417\t\n418\t\n419\t(defn- frame-record\n420\t  [bs]\n421\t  (try\n422\t    (::journal/value (cbor/decode bs))\n423\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n424\t\n425\t\n426\t(defn- fail-hit!\n427\t  \"Whether the life's uncertain-append failure ({:like cut-name\n428\t   :persist? bool}) matches this write at `site`: the first match only.\"\n429\t  [ctx site subject]\n430\t  (when-some [{:keys [like]} (:fail ctx)]\n431\t    (let [spec (get cuts like)]\n432\t      (when (and (nil? @(:failed ctx))\n433\t                 (= site (:site spec))\n434\t                 ((:match spec) subject))\n435\t        (reset! (:failed ctx) {:site site :like like})\n436\t        true))))\n437\t\n438\t\n439\t(defn mortal-backend\n440\t  \"Journal backend `b` at `site`, mortal under `ctx`: once the life is\n441\t   dead every frame write throws having written nothing, and the life's\n442\t   cut, when it names this site, fires before or after its frame.\"\n443\t  [ctx site b]\n444\t  (swap! (:opened ctx) conj [:backend b])\n445\t  (let [write! (::journal/write-frame! b)\n446\t        truncate! (::journal/truncate! b)]\n447\t    (assoc b\n448\t           ::journal/write-frame!\n449\t           (fn [bs]\n450\t             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n451\t             (when (fail-hit! ctx site (frame-record bs))\n452\t               ;; an uncertain append: the frame lands or not, and the\n453\t               ;; writer is answered a throw either way -- the process\n454\t               ;; lives on, its journal's answer unknown\n455\t               (when (:persist? (:fail ctx)) (write! bs))\n456\t               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :uncertain :site site\n457\t                              :persisted? (boolean (:persist? (:fail ctx)))\n458\t                              :record (->data (frame-record bs))})\n459\t               (throw (ex-info \"stage E: an uncertain append\" {::uncertain true})))\n460\t             (let [hit (hit! ctx site (frame-record bs))]\n461\t               (when (= :before hit)\n462\t                 (fire! ctx {:site site :when :before\n463\t                             :record (->data (frame-record bs))}))\n464\t               (let [r (write! bs)]\n465\t                 (when (= :after hit)\n466\t                   (fire! ctx {:site site :when :after\n467\t                               :record (->data (frame-record bs))}))\n468\t                 r)))\n469\t           ::journal/truncate!\n470\t           (fn [n]\n471\t             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n472\t             (truncate! n)))))\n473\t\n474\t\n475\t(defn mortal-store\n476\t  \"Content store `base`, mortal under `ctx`, its puts cut at :store; its\n477\t   gets answer the default for every address in `unreadable` (an\n478\t   accepted checkpoint whose bytes cannot be read).\"\n479\t  [ctx base unreadable]\n480\t  (swap! (:opened ctx) conj [:store base])\n481\t  (let [put! (:put-bytes-fn base)\n482\t        get! (:get-bytes-fn base)]\n483\t    (assoc base\n484\t           :put-bytes-fn\n485\t           (fn [address bs]\n486\t             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n487\t             (let [hit (hit! ctx :store {:address address})]\n488\t               (when (= :before hit)\n489\t                 (fire! ctx {:site :store :when :before :address address}))\n490\t               (let [r (put! address bs)]\n491\t                 (when (= :after hit)\n492\t                   (fire! ctx {:site :store :when :after :address address}))\n493\t                 r)))\n494\t           :get-bytes-fn\n495\t           (fn\n496\t             ([address] (get! address))\n497\t             ([address default]\n498\t              (if (contains? unreadable address)\n499\t                default\n500\t                (get! address default)))))))\n501\t\n502\t\n503\t(defn- open-file-backend!\n504\t  [dir]\n505\t  (ensure-dir! dir)\n506\t  (let [r (file-journal/backend! dir)]\n507\t    (or (::file-journal/backend r)\n508\t        (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a durable journal directory refused\"\n509\t                        {:dir dir :answer r})))))\n510\t\n511\t\n512\t(defn- mortal-journals\n513\t  \"compose/file-journals over `root`, every backend it opens mortal at\n514\t   [:progress h] or [:reply h].\"\n515\t  [ctx root]\n516\t  (let [base (compose/file-journals root)]\n517\t    (assoc base\n518\t           :progress-backend!\n519\t           (fn [h] (mortal-backend ctx [:progress h] ((:progress-backend! base) h)))\n520\t           :reply-backend!\n521\t           (fn [h] (mortal-backend ctx [:reply h] ((:reply-backend! base) h))))))\n522\t\n523\t\n524\t;; =============================================================================\n525\t;; Streams outside custody\n526\t;; =============================================================================\n527\t\n528\t\n529\t(defn scenario-stream\n530\t  \"A stream outside custody, rebuilt by every life under its fixed\n531\t   `identity`: `values` at integer positions from zero, positions below\n532\t   `floor` evicted (their reads answer gap with the floor as the\n533\t   successor cursor).  Integer positions make a position lifted from one\n534\t   life's instance a valid cursor on the next life's.\"\n535\t  [identity values floor]\n536\t  (let [vs (atom (vec values))]\n537\t    (reify\n538\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n539\t      (descriptor\n540\t        [_]\n541\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n542\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n543\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n544\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n545\t\n546\t\n547\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n548\t\n549\t      (cursor\n550\t        [_ _anchor]\n551\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor floor})\n552\t\n553\t      (next\n554\t        [_ cursor]\n555\t        (let [values @vs]\n556\t          (cond\n557\t            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count values))))\n558\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n559\t            (< cursor floor)\n560\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/cursor floor}\n561\t            (< cursor (count values))\n562\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n563\t             :dao.stream/value (nth values cursor)\n564\t             :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n565\t            :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n566\t\n567\t\n568\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n569\t\n570\t      (append!\n571\t        [_ x]\n572\t        (swap! vs conj x)\n573\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n574\t\n575\t\n576\t(defn journal-stream\n577\t  \"A durable stream over journal handle `j` under the fixed `identity`:\n578\t   integer positions over the journal's own, so every life reads the\n579\t   whole history any life appended -- the side log of at-least-once\n580\t   external IO.\"\n581\t  [identity j]\n582\t  (let [jid (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor j))]\n583\t    (reify\n584\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n585\t      (descriptor\n586\t        [_]\n587\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n588\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n589\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n590\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n591\t\n592\t\n593\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n594\t\n595\t      (cursor\n596\t        [_ _anchor]\n597\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n598\t\n599\t      (next\n600\t        [_ cursor]\n601\t        (if-not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor))\n602\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n603\t          (let [r (stream/next j {:dao.stream.memory-log/identity jid\n604\t                                  :dao.stream.memory-log/position cursor})]\n605\t            (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n606\t              :dao.stream/ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n607\t                              :dao.stream/value (:dao.stream/value r)\n608\t                              :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n609\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n610\t\n611\t\n612\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n613\t\n614\t      (append!\n615\t        [_ x]\n616\t        (stream/append! j x)))))\n617\t\n618\t\n619\t(defn- answering-inbound\n620\t  \"A log-shaped inbound whose appends answer `@outcome`: :dao.stream/ok\n621\t   lands the request; any other outcome lands nothing (the carrier full,\n622\t   refusing, or failing under the send).\"\n623\t  [identity outcome]\n624\t  (let [values (atom [])]\n625\t    (reify\n626\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n627\t      (descriptor\n628\t        [_]\n629\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n630\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n631\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n632\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n633\t\n634\t\n635\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n636\t\n637\t      (cursor\n638\t        [_ _anchor]\n639\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n640\t\n641\t      (next\n642\t        [_ cursor]\n643\t        (let [vs @values]\n644\t          (cond\n645\t            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n646\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n647\t            (< cursor (count vs))\n648\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n649\t             :dao.stream/value (nth vs cursor)\n650\t             :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n651\t            :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n652\t\n653\t\n654\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n655\t\n656\t      (append!\n657\t        [_ x]\n658\t        (let [o @outcome]\n659\t          (when (= :dao.stream/ok o) (swap! values conj x))\n660\t          {:dao.stream/outcome o})))))\n661\t\n662\t\n663\t(defn- held-inbound\n664\t  \"A log-shaped inbound whose reads answer :blocked while `held` (an\n665\t   atom) is truthy: the holder's requests land, but the authority's\n666\t   front cannot read them -- the holder partitioned from its\n667\t   authority.  Healed, the front reads every request that landed.\"\n668\t  [identity held]\n669\t  (let [values (atom [])]\n670\t    (reify\n671\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n672\t      (descriptor\n673\t        [_]\n674\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n675\t         :dao.stream/identity identity\n676\t         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n677\t                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n678\t\n679\t\n680\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n681\t\n682\t      (cursor\n683\t        [_ _anchor]\n684\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n685\t\n686\t      (next\n687\t        [_ cursor]\n688\t        (if @held\n689\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}\n690\t          (let [vs @values]\n691\t            (cond\n692\t              (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n693\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n694\t              (< cursor (count vs))\n695\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n696\t               :dao.stream/value (nth vs cursor)\n697\t               :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n698\t              :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n699\t\n700\t\n701\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n702\t\n703\t      (append!\n704\t        [_ x]\n705\t        (swap! values conj x)\n706\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n707\t\n708\t\n709\t(defn- log-writer\n710\t  []\n711\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n712\t    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log})))\n713\t\n714\t\n715\t;; =============================================================================\n716\t;; Machines and holder seams\n717\t;; =============================================================================\n718\t\n719\t\n720\t(def prog-id \"prog-c\")\n721\t(def source-id \"src-s\")\n722\t(def side-id \"side-x\")\n723\t\n724\t\n725\t(defn- parked-reader-over\n726\t  \"A real gated machine over `source`, parked on its first read: one\n727\t   more delivered value and it halts with :done.\"\n728\t  [source]\n729\t  (let [m0 (s/load-ast (s/new-machine)\n730\t                       (s/then {:type :stream/next, :source (s/v 'c)}\n731\t                               (s/lit :done)))\n732\t        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n733\t        [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)]\n734\t    (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'c cref} :yin.k/gate :running))))\n735\t\n736\t\n737\t(defn- reading-writer\n738\t  \"A real gated machine over `source`, parked on its first read: the\n739\t   value it reads is written to the enrolled `target`, then :side to\n740\t   `side`, then it halts with :done.\"\n741\t  [source target side]\n742\t  (let [m0 (s/load-ast (s/new-machine)\n743\t                       (s/let1 'v (s/next-of (s/v 'c))\n744\t                               (s/then {:type :stream/put, :target (s/v 'w),\n745\t                                        :val (s/v 'v)}\n746\t                                       (s/then {:type :stream/put,\n747\t                                                :target (s/v 'x),\n748\t                                                :val (s/lit :side)}\n749\t                                               (s/lit :done)))))\n750\t        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n751\t        [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)\n752\t        [wref m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 target)\n753\t        [xref m4] (engine/attach-resource m3 side)]\n754\t    (vm/run (assoc m4 :store {'c cref, 'w wref, 'x xref}\n755\t                   :yin.k/gate :running))))\n756\t\n757\t\n758\t(defn- attach-over\n759\t  [ctx table]\n760\t  (fn [descriptor]\n761\t    (swap! (:attaches ctx) inc)\n762\t    (if-some [h (get table (:dao.stream/identity descriptor))]\n763\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/handle h}\n764\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found})))\n765\t\n766\t\n767\t(defn- observe-over\n768\t  [ctx]\n769\t  (fn [h op arg]\n770\t    (swap! (:observes ctx) inc)\n771\t    (case op\n772\t      :next (stream/next h arg)\n773\t      :cursor (stream/cursor h arg))))\n774\t\n775\t\n776\t(defn- same-id-server\n777\t  []\n778\t  (fn [h]\n779\t    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor h))]\n780\t      {:dao.stream/identity id\n781\t       :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n782\t                            :dao.stream/identity id}})))\n783\t\n784\t\n785\t;; =============================================================================\n786\t;; Opening a life's world\n787\t;; =============================================================================\n788\t\n789\t\n790\t(defn- composition-config\n791\t  [w mode]\n792\t  (cond-> {:mode mode\n793\t           :source-index (fn [] @s/source-index)\n794\t           :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n795\t           :store (:store w)\n796\t           :diagnostics (:diagnostics w)\n797\t           :medium \"stage-e\"\n798\t           :clock (fn [] {:s @(:clock w)})}\n799\t    (= :exclusive mode) (assoc :failure-model :process-crash\n800\t                               :backend (:authority-backend w)\n801\t                               :duration {:s 30}\n802\t                               :journals (:journals w))))\n803\t\n804\t\n805\t(defn- world-table\n806\t  \"The holder table and protection of the life's world kind.\"\n807\t  [w]\n808\t  (case (:kind w)\n809\t    :parked {:table (if (= :none (:attach w)) {} {prog-id (:prog w)})\n810\t             :protection {prog-id :at-least-once}}\n811\t    :rows {:table (cond-> {source-id (:source w) side-id (:side w)}\n812\t                    (:target w) (assoc (:target w) (:reader w)))\n813\t           :protection (cond-> {source-id :at-least-once side-id :at-least-once}\n814\t                         (:target w) (assoc (:target w) :enrolled))}))\n815\t\n816\t\n817\t(defn- holder-seams\n818\t  [ctx w]\n819\t  (let [{:keys [table protection]} (world-table w)]\n820\t    {:protection protection\n821\t     :receiver (s/new-machine)\n822\t     :attach! (attach-over ctx table)\n823\t     :observe! (observe-over ctx)\n824\t     :serve! (if (= :parked (:kind w))\n825\t               (fn [_h]\n826\t                 {:dao.stream/identity prog-id\n827\t                  :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n828\t                                       :dao.stream/identity prog-id}})\n829\t               (same-id-server))}))\n830\t\n831\t\n832\t(defn- source-machine\n833\t  [w]\n834\t  (case (:kind w)\n835\t    :parked (parked-reader-over (scenario-stream prog-id [] 0))\n836\t    :rows (reading-writer (:source w) (:reader w) (:side w))))\n837\t\n838\t\n839\t(defn open-world!\n840\t  \"Open the life's world over `spec`: the durable media, mortal under\n841\t   `ctx`, and the composition over them.  Answers the world map with\n842\t   :c the open composition, or :refusal the composition's data refusal.\"\n843\t  [ctx spec]\n844\t  (let [{:keys [root kind mode]} spec\n845\t        mode (or mode :exclusive)\n846\t        p (paths root)\n847\t        _ (ensure-dir! root)\n848\t        partitioned (atom false)\n849\t        authority-backend (when (= :exclusive mode)\n850\t                            (let [b (mortal-backend ctx :authority\n851\t                                                    (open-file-backend! (:authority p)))\n852\t                                  write! (::journal/write-frame! b)]\n853\t                              ;; the protected consumer partitioned from\n854\t                              ;; its authority: every frame write fails\n855\t                              ;; while the flag stands\n856\t                              (assoc b ::journal/write-frame!\n857\t                                     (fn [bs]\n858\t                                       (if @partitioned\n859\t                                         (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the authority is partitioned\" {}))\n860\t                                         (write! bs))))))\n861\t        store (mortal-store ctx (jing-file/create-content-file (:store p))\n862\t                            (set (:unreadable spec)))\n863\t        side-backend (when (= :rows kind)\n864\t                       (mortal-backend ctx :side (open-file-backend! (:side p))))\n865\t        side (when side-backend\n866\t               (journal-stream side-id (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! side-backend nil))))\n867\t        w {:root root\n868\t           :kind kind\n869\t           :mode mode\n870\t           :attach (:attach spec)\n871\t           :clock (atom (or (:clock spec) 1))\n872\t           :store store\n873\t           :diagnostics (log-writer)\n874\t           :authority-backend authority-backend\n875\t           :side-backend side-backend\n876\t           :journals (if (= :exclusive mode)\n877\t                       (mortal-journals ctx (:journals p))\n878\t                       (compose/memory-journals (atom {})))\n879\t           :prog (scenario-stream prog-id (or (:prog spec) []) 0)\n880\t           :source (scenario-stream source-id (or (:source spec) [\"A\"])\n881\t                                    (or (:evict-floor spec) 0))\n882\t           :side side\n883\t           :partitioned partitioned\n884\t           :carrier (atom :dao.stream/ok)\n885\t           :held (atom false)\n886\t           :inbound (:inbound spec)}\n887\t        opened (compose/open! (composition-config w mode))\n888\t        c (:yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition opened)]\n889\t    (if (nil? c)\n890\t      (assoc w :refusal (->data opened))\n891\t      (let [w (assoc w :c c)]\n892\t        (if (= :rows kind)\n893\t          (let [i (or (:target spec)\n894\t                      (let [e (compose/enroll! c)]\n895\t                        ((:emit! ctx) {:event :enrolled :target (:yin.k/target e)})\n896\t                        (:yin.k/target e)))]\n897\t            (assoc w :target i :reader (compose/target-reader c i)))\n898\t          w)))))\n899\t\n900\t\n901\t(defn release-dead!\n902\t  \"What the operating system does for a killed process, done for a life\n903\t   killed in this process: every file backend and the store it opened\n904\t   released, nothing written.\"\n905\t  [ctx]\n906\t  (doseq [[kind x] @(:opened ctx)]\n907\t    (try\n908\t      (case kind\n909\t        :backend (when (contains? x ::file-journal/close!) (file-journal/close! x))\n910\t        :store ((:close-fn x)))\n911\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n912\t\n913\t\n914\t(defn close-world!\n915\t  \"Release everything a live world holds: the composition (its journal\n916\t   backends), the authority backend, the side log and the store.\"\n917\t  [w]\n918\t  (let [safe (fn [f]\n919\t               (try (f) (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))]\n920\t    (when-some [c (:c w)] (safe #(compose/close! c)))\n921\t    (when-some [b (:authority-backend w)] (safe #(file-journal/close! b)))\n922\t    (when-some [b (:side-backend w)] (safe #(file-journal/close! b)))\n923\t    (when-some [close! (get-in w [:store :close-fn])] (safe close!))\n924\t    nil))\n925\t\n926\t\n927\t;; =============================================================================\n928\t;; Reading a live world\n929\t;; =============================================================================\n930\t\n931\t\n932\t(defn- journal-values\n933\t  [j]\n934\t  (if (nil? j)\n935\t    []\n936\t    (read-values j)))\n937\t\n938\t\n939\t(defn replies-of\n940\t  \"Every reply the composition's front wrote into holder `h`'s reply\n941\t   journal (both tenures': the journal is durable).\"\n942\t  [c h]\n943\t  (journal-values (get-in c [:reply-journals h :journal])))\n944\t\n945\t\n946\t(defn holder-summary\n947\t  [st]\n948\t  (->data (merge (select-keys st [:phase :status :detail :occurrence :lease])\n949\t                 {:epoch (get-in st [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch])\n950\t                  :next-op-seq (get-in st [:machine :yin.k/custody :yin.k/next-op-seq])\n951\t                  :stopped? (:stopped? st)\n952\t                  :machine? (some? (:machine st))})))\n953\t\n954\t\n955\t(defn snapshot\n956\t  \"Everything a check may read of the live world, as data.\"\n957\t  [ctx w]\n958\t  (let [c (:c w)\n959\t        hs (sort (keys (:holders c)))]\n960\t    {:holders (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (holder-summary (get-in c [:holders h]))])) hs)\n961\t     :policy (:yin.k/policy c)\n962\t     :projection (->data (projection-of c))\n963\t     :journals (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (journal-records-of c h))])) hs)\n964\t     :replies (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (replies-of c h))])) hs)\n965\t     :inbound (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (inbound-of c h nil))])) hs)\n966\t     :targets (if-some [i (:target w)]\n967\t                {:target (->data i)\n968\t                 :values (->data (read-values (compose/target-reader c i)))}\n969\t                {})\n970\t     :outcomes (if-some [r (compose/outcome-reader c)]\n971\t                 (->data (read-values r))\n972\t                 [])\n973\t     :side (if-some [side (:side w)] (->data (read-values side)) [])\n974\t     :fences (into {}\n975\t                   (keep (fn [r]\n976\t                           (when (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n977\t                             (let [a (:yin.k/address r)\n978\t                                   bs ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) a nil)]\n979\t                               [a (when bs (digest-of bs))]))))\n980\t                   (mapcat #(journal-records-of c %) hs))\n981\t     :packs (into {}\n982\t                  (keep (fn [r]\n983\t                          (when (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n984\t                            (let [a (:yin.k/address r)\n985\t                                  bs ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) a nil)]\n986\t                              (when bs\n987\t                                (let [wire (cbor/decode bs)]\n988\t                                  [a {:root (:yin.k/root wire)\n989\t                                      :baseline (checkpoint/inspect a bs)\n990\t                                      :sorted? (= (mapv first (:yin.k/rows wire))\n991\t                                                  (vec (sort (map first (:yin.k/rows wire)))))\n992\t                                      :canonical-bytes (digest-of (cbor/encode (rows/emit (rows/decode wire))))}]))))))\n993\t                  (mapcat #(journal-records-of c %) hs))\n994\t     :diagnostics (->data (read-values (:diagnostics w)))\n995\t     :arbitration (->data (compose/arbitration c))\n996\t     :counts {:attaches @(:attaches ctx) :observes @(:observes ctx)}\n997\t     :clock @(:clock w)}))\n998\t\n999\t\n1000\t;; =============================================================================\n1001\t;; The life's program: plain-data operations over the composition\n1002\t;; =============================================================================\n1003\t\n1004\t\n1005\t(defn- durable-records\n1006\t  \"Holder `h`'s progress journal: through the composition when this life\n1007\t   composes `h`, else read from its durable directory (a holder a\n1008\t   previous life ran).\"\n1009\t  [w h]\n1010\t  (if (contains? (get-in w [:c :holders]) h)\n1011\t    (journal-records-of (:c w) h)\n1012\t    (let [b (open-file-backend! (str (:journals (paths (:root w))) \"/\" h \"-progress\"))]\n1013\t      (try\n1014\t        (journal-values (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! b nil)))\n1015\t        (finally (file-journal/close! b))))))\n1016\t\n1017\t\n1018\t(defn- checkpoint-from\n1019\t  \"The checkpoint a candidate is added over, read from the durable\n1020\t   journal of `of` and the store: :fence the source's export, :successor\n1021\t   the exit's successor, or an explicit {:address a}.\"\n1022\t  [w {:keys [kind of address]}]\n1023\t  (let [records (durable-records w of)\n1024\t        fence (fn [o]\n1025\t                (some (fn [r]\n1026\t                        (when (and (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n1027\t                                   (or (nil? o) (= o (:yin.k/occurrence r))))\n1028\t                          r))\n1029\t                      records))\n1030\t        address (case kind\n1031\t                  :fence (:yin.k/address (fence nil))\n1032\t                  :successor (let [mint (last (filter\n1033\t                                                (fn [r]\n1034\t                                                  (and (= :yin.k/minted (:yin.k/journal r))\n1035\t                                                       (= :yin.k/successor (:yin.k/role r))))\n1036\t                                                records))]\n1037\t                               (:yin.k/address (fence (:yin.k/occurrence mint))))\n1038\t                  :variant (:address (:variant w))\n1039\t                  :address address)\n1040\t        bs (when address ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) address nil))]\n1041\t    (when (nil? bs)\n1042\t      (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the checkpoint is absent from the store\"\n1043\t                      {:checkpoint {:kind kind :of of :address (->data address)}})))\n1044\t    {:address address :bytes bs}))\n1045\t\n1046\t\n1047\t(defn- inbound-for\n1048\t  \"Holder `h`'s inbound, when the life's spec names one: :answering, a\n1049\t   carrier whose appends answer the life's carrier outcome; :held, a\n1050\t   stream the front cannot read while the life holds the partition.\"\n1051\t  [w h]\n1052\t  (case (get (:inbound w) h)\n1053\t    :answering {:inbound (answering-inbound (str \"inbound-\" h) (:carrier w))}\n1054\t    :held {:inbound (held-inbound (str \"inbound-\" h) (:held w))}\n1055\t    nil))\n1056\t\n1057\t\n1058\t(defn- offer-variant!\n1059\t  \"A second encoding of the occurrence holder `h` fenced: the same root\n1060\t   with reversed rows in different canonical bytes, put in the store\n1061\t   and offered through `h`'s own inbound.  Answers {:address :bytes}.\"\n1062\t  [w h]\n1063\t  (let [{:keys [address bytes]} (checkpoint-from w {:kind :fence :of h})\n1064\t        body (cbor/decode bytes)\n1065\t        o (:yin.k/occurrence (checkpoint/inspect address bytes))\n1066\t        v-bytes (cbor/encode (update body :yin.k/rows #(vec (reverse %))))\n1067\t        v-address (rows/pack-address (cbor/decode v-bytes))]\n1068\t    ((:put-bytes-fn (:store w)) v-address v-bytes)\n1069\t    (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h])\n1070\t                    {:yin.k/request :yin.k/offer\n1071\t                     :yin.k/request-id [:stage-e/variant (str address)]\n1072\t                     :yin.k/id v-address\n1073\t                     :yin.k/bytes v-bytes\n1074\t                     :yin.k/medium \"stage-e\"})\n1075\t    {:address v-address :bytes v-bytes :occurrence o}))\n1076\t\n1077\t\n1078\t(defn- holder-config\n1079\t  [ctx w extra]\n1080\t  (merge (holder-seams ctx w) extra))\n1081\t\n1082\t\n1083\t(defn- add-source\n1084\t  [ctx w h]\n1085\t  (update w :c compose/source h (holder-config ctx w (merge {:machine (source-machine w)}\n1086\t                                                            (inbound-for w h)))))\n1087\t\n1088\t\n1089\t(defn- add-candidate\n1090\t  [ctx w h checkpoint opts]\n1091\t  (let [{:keys [address bytes]} (checkpoint-from w checkpoint)\n1092\t        seams (holder-config ctx w (merge {:bytes bytes :address address}\n1093\t                                          (inbound-for w h)))\n1094\t        seams (if (= :none (:attach opts))\n1095\t                (assoc seams :attach! (fn [_] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found}))\n1096\t                seams)]\n1097\t    (update w :c compose/holder h seams)))\n1098\t\n1099\t\n1100\t(defn- dead?\n1101\t  [ctx]\n1102\t  @(:dead ctx))\n1103\t\n1104\t\n1105\t(defn- tick!\n1106\t  \"One tick of `f` over the world's composition; the life's tick cut is\n1107\t   checked after it.  A dead life ends here.\"\n1108\t  [ctx w f]\n1109\t  (let [c' (f (:c w))\n1110\t        w (assoc w :c c')]\n1111\t    (when (dead? ctx) (dead-throw!))\n1112\t    (let [spec (cut-spec ctx)]\n1113\t      (when (and (some? spec) (= :tick (:site spec)) (nil? @(:fired ctx))\n1114\t                 ((:match spec) c'))\n1115\t        (fire! ctx {:site :tick\n1116\t                    :holders (into {} (map (fn [[h st]] [h (holder-summary st)])) (:holders c'))\n1117\t                    :inbound (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (inbound-of c' h nil))]))\n1118\t                                   (keys (:holders c')))})))\n1119\t    w))\n1120\t\n1121\t\n1122\t(def ^:private planes\n1123\t  {:step compose/step\n1124\t   :control compose/control-step\n1125\t   :program compose/program-step})\n1126\t\n1127\t\n1128\t(defn- phase?\n1129\t  [w h phase]\n1130\t  (= phase (get-in w [:c :holders h :phase])))\n1131\t\n1132\t\n1133\t(defn- until\n1134\t  \"Ticks of `plane` until `pred` holds of the world or `n` are spent;\n1135\t   answers [world held?].\"\n1136\t  [ctx w plane pred n]\n1137\t  (loop [w w k 0]\n1138\t    (if (pred w)\n1139\t      [w true]\n1140\t      (if (>= k n)\n1141\t        [w false]\n1142\t        (recur (tick! ctx w (get planes plane)) (inc k))))))\n1143\t\n1144\t\n1145\t(defn- admit-request\n1146\t  [rid target envelope]\n1147\t  {:yin.k/request :yin.k/admit\n1148\t   :yin.k/request-id rid\n1149\t   :yin.k/target target\n1150\t   :yin.k/fenced-envelope envelope})\n1151\t\n1152\t\n1153\t(defn- envelope\n1154\t  [lease epoch op-id value]\n1155\t  {:yin.k/envelope :yin.k/fenced-v1\n1156\t   :yin.k/incarnation lease\n1157\t   :yin.k/epoch epoch\n1158\t   :yin.k/op-id op-id\n1159\t   :yin.k/value value})\n1160\t\n1161\t\n1162\t(defn- holder-binding\n1163\t  [w h]\n1164\t  (let [st (get-in w [:c :holders h])]\n1165\t    {:lease (:lease st)\n1166\t     :epoch (get-in st [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch])\n1167\t     :occurrence (:occurrence st)}))\n1168\t\n1169\t\n1170\t(defn- resolve-arg\n1171\t  \"Operation arguments may name a holder's live binding: [:binding h k].\"\n1172\t  [w x]\n1173\t  (if (and (vector? x) (= :binding (first x)))\n1174\t    (get (holder-binding w (nth x 1)) (nth x 2))\n1175\t    x))\n1176\t\n1177\t\n1178\t(defn- admit!\n1179\t  \"Append an authored admit to holder `h`'s inbound and run control ticks\n1180\t   until its reply lands (or `n` are spent).\"\n1181\t  [ctx w h {:keys [rid target lease epoch op-id value await?]}]\n1182\t  (let [target (cond (= :other target) (:other w)\n1183\t                     (some? target) (resolve-arg w target)\n1184\t                     :else (:target w))\n1185\t        lease (resolve-arg w lease)\n1186\t        epoch (resolve-arg w epoch)\n1187\t        op-id (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (resolve-arg w v)])) op-id)\n1188\t        n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n1189\t    (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h])\n1190\t                    (admit-request rid target (envelope lease epoch op-id value)))\n1191\t    (if (false? await?)\n1192\t      (tick! ctx w compose/control-step)\n1193\t      (first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)))))\n1194\t\n1195\t\n1196\t(defn- run-op\n1197\t  \"One operation of a life's program; answers [world report-additions].\"\n1198\t  [ctx w [op & args]]\n1199\t  (case op\n1200\t    :source [(add-source ctx w (first args)) nil]\n1201\t    :candidate (let [[h checkpoint opts] args]\n1202\t                 [(add-candidate ctx w h checkpoint opts) nil])\n1203\t    :until (let [[h phase n plane] args\n1204\t                 [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step) #(phase? % h phase) n)]\n1205\t             [w {:until [[h phase held?]]}])\n1206\t    :until-status (let [[h status n] args\n1207\t                        [w held?] (until ctx w :step\n1208\t                                         #(= status (get-in % [:c :holders h :status])) n)]\n1209\t                    [w {:until [[h status held?]]}])\n1210\t    :until-inbound (let [[h kind n plane] args\n1211\t                         [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n1212\t                                          #(seq (inbound-of (:c %) h kind)) n)]\n1213\t                     [w {:until [[h kind held?]]}])\n1214\t    :until-reply (let [[h kind n plane] args\n1215\t                       [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n1216\t                                        #(some (fn [r] (= kind (:yin.k/reply r)))\n1217\t                                               (replies-of (:c %) h))\n1218\t                                        n)]\n1219\t                   [w {:until [[h kind held?]]}])\n1220\t    :until-some (let [[phase n] args\n1221\t                      [w held?] (until ctx w :step\n1222\t                                       (fn [w]\n1223\t                                         (some #(= phase (:phase %))\n1224\t                                               (vals (get-in w [:c :holders]))))\n1225\t                                       n)]\n1226\t                  [w {:until [[:some phase held?]]}])\n1227\t    :until-journal (let [[h kind action n plane] args\n1228\t                         [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n1229\t                                          #(holder-records-match?\n1230\t                                             (:c %) h (record-is kind action))\n1231\t                                          n)]\n1232\t                     [w {:until [[h kind action held?]]}])\n1233\t    :ticks (let [[n plane] args]\n1234\t             [(reduce (fn [w _] (tick! ctx w (get planes (or plane :step)))) w (range n)) nil])\n1235\t    :hand-off [(update w :c compose/hand-off (first args)) nil]\n1236\t    :abort [(update w :c compose/abort (first args)) nil]\n1237\t    :clock (do (reset! (:clock w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1238\t    :append-prog (do (stream/append! (:prog w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1239\t    :admit (let [[h req] args] [(admit! ctx w h req) nil])\n1240\t    :enroll-other (let [e (compose/enroll! (:c w))]\n1241\t                    [(assoc w :other (:yin.k/target e)) {:other (->data (:yin.k/target e))}])\n1242\t    :snapshot (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n1243\t                ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key (first args) :snapshot snap})\n1244\t                [w {:snapshots {(first args) snap}}])\n1245\t    :binding (let [b (->data (holder-binding w (first args)))]\n1246\t               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :binding :holder (first args) :binding b})\n1247\t               [w {:bindings {(first args) b}}])\n1248\t    :inject (let [[h request] args\n1249\t                  n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n1250\t              (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h]) request)\n1251\t              [(first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)) nil])\n1252\t    :offer-variant (let [[h] args\n1253\t                         v (offer-variant! w h)]\n1254\t                     ((:emit! ctx) {:event :variant :address (:address v)})\n1255\t                     [(assoc w :variant v) {:variant (->data (:address v))\n1256\t                                            :variant-baseline (checkpoint/inspect (:address v) (:bytes v))}])\n1257\t    :carrier (do (reset! (:carrier w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1258\t    :hold (do (reset! (:held w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1259\t    :partition-authority (do (reset! (:partitioned w) (first args)) [w nil])\n1260\t    :die (fire! ctx {:site :explicit :at (first args)})\n1261\t    :at-open (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n1262\t               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key :at-open :snapshot snap})\n1263\t               [w {:at-open snap}])))\n1264\t\n1265\t\n1266\t(defn- merge-report\n1267\t  [report additions]\n1268\t  (merge-with (fn [a b] (if (and (map? a) (map? b)) (merge a b) (into a b)))\n1269\t              report additions))\n1270\t\n1271\t\n1272\t(defn- fork-row\n1273\t  \"A fork per host: fork runs when selected and is labelled fork, and an\n1274\t   exclusive requirement over a memory authority is refused, never\n1275\t   downgraded.\"\n1276\t  [ctx spec]\n1277\t  (let [refused (compose/open! {:source-index (fn [] @s/source-index)\n1278\t                                :mode :exclusive\n1279\t                                :failure-model :process-crash\n1280\t                                :backend (journal/memory-backend (atom []) nil)\n1281\t                                :duration {:s 30}\n1282\t                                :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n1283\t                                :store (jing-file/create-content-file\n1284\t                                         (str (:root spec) \"/refused.jing\"))\n1285\t                                :diagnostics (log-writer)\n1286\t                                :medium \"stage-e\"\n1287\t                                :clock (fn [] {:s 1})\n1288\t                                :journals (compose/file-journals\n1289\t                                            (str (:root spec) \"/refused\"))})\n1290\t        w (open-world! ctx (assoc spec :mode :fork :kind :parked))]\n1291\t    (try\n1292\t      (let [w (add-source ctx w \"h1\")\n1293\t            [w held?] (until ctx w :step #(phase? % \"h1\" :lifted) 12)]\n1294\t        {:refused (->data (dissoc refused :yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition))\n1295\t         :refused-composed? (some? (:yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition refused))\n1296\t         :fork {:held? held?\n1297\t                :policy (:yin.k/policy (:c w))\n1298\t                :status-policy (:yin.k/policy (compose/status (:c w)))\n1299\t                :arbitration (->data (compose/arbitration (:c w)))\n1300\t                :holder (holder-summary (get-in w [:c :holders \"h1\"]))\n1301\t                :address (->data (get-in w [:c :holders \"h1\" :detail :yin.k/address]))\n1302\t                :journal (->data (journal-records-of (:c w) \"h1\"))\n1303\t                :offers (->data (inbound-of (:c w) \"h1\" :yin.k/offer))\n1304\t                :fronts (count (:fronts (:c w)))\n1305\t                :outcome-reader? (some? (compose/outcome-reader (:c w)))}})\n1306\t      (finally (close-world! w)))))\n1307\t\n1308\t\n1309\t(defn run-life\n1310\t  \"Run one life of `spec` under `ctx` and answer its report (plain data).\n1311\t\n1312\t   spec:\n1313\t     :root     the scenario root (the durable media)\n1314\t     :kind     :parked (the parked-reader source of rows 1, 2, 6, 7) or\n1315\t               :rows (the reading-writer source over an enrolled target\n1316\t               of rows 3, 4, 5, 8)\n1317\t     :target   the enrolled target a :rows life reuses (absent: enroll,\n1318\t               emitting {:event :enrolled})\n1319\t     :clock    the life's starting clock reading, in seconds\n1320\t     :prog     the program stream's values this life sees\n1321\t     :source   the source stream's values; :evict-floor its eviction\n1322\t     :unreadable addresses the store cannot read\n1323\t     :attach   :none for an attach table that holds nothing\n1324\t     :ops      the life's program, a vector of operations (run-op)\n1325\t     :lose-authority true to destroy the authority's state first\n1326\t     :fork-row true for the per-host fork row instead\n1327\t\n1328\t   The cut, when any, is the context's.  A dead life throws ::killed\n1329\t   out of here; the caller (peer or in-process runner) decides what a\n1330\t   kill means.\"\n1331\t  [ctx spec]\n1332\t  (when (:lose-authority spec)\n1333\t    (destroy-authority! (:root spec)))\n1334\t  (cond\n1335\t    (:fork-row spec)\n1336\t    (fork-row ctx spec)\n1337\t\n1338\t    ;; a lost ledger the durable backend itself refuses to open never\n1339\t    ;; reaches the composition: fail stop, reported as data\n1340\t    (and (:lose-authority spec)\n1341\t         (not= :dao.stream/ok\n1342\t               (:dao.stream/outcome\n1343\t                 (let [r (file-journal/backend! (:authority (paths (:root spec))))]\n1344\t                   (when-some [b (::file-journal/backend r)] (file-journal/close! b))\n1345\t                   r))))\n1346\t    {:refusal {:stage :authority-backend\n1347\t               :answer (->data (file-journal/backend! (:authority (paths (:root spec)))))}}\n1348\t\n1349\t    :else\n1350\t    (let [w (open-world! ctx spec)]\n1351\t      (if-some [refusal (:refusal w)]\n1352\t        (do (close-world! w)\n1353\t            {:refusal refusal})\n1354\t        (let [result (atom w)]\n1355\t          (try\n1356\t            (let [[w report] (reduce (fn [[w report] op]\n1357\t                                       (let [[w additions] (run-op ctx w op)]\n1358\t                                         (reset! result w)\n1359\t                                         [w (merge-report report additions)]))\n1360\t                                     [w {}]\n1361\t                                     (:ops spec))]\n1362\t              (reset! result w)\n1363\t              (assoc report :final (snapshot ctx w)))\n1364\t            (finally\n1365\t              (when-not (dead? ctx)\n1366\t                (close-world! @result)))))))))\n1367\t\n1368\t\n1369\t;; =============================================================================\n1370\t;; Inspection: the durable state after every life, read without mutating it\n1371\t;; =============================================================================\n1372\t\n1373\t\n1374\t(defn inspect\n1375\t  \"Read the durable state under `root` without mutating it: the\n1376\t   authority's projection through `authority/open!` (no reclaim, unlike\n1377\t   the grantor's reopen), the enrolled `targets`' committed values, the\n1378\t   outcome projection, each holder's progress and reply journal, and the\n1379\t   side log.\"\n1380\t  [{:keys [root holders targets]}]\n1381\t  (let [p (paths root)\n1382\t        backend (::file-journal/backend (file-journal/backend! (:authority p)))\n1383\t        opened (if backend (authority/open! backend nil) {:yin.k/status :backend-refused})\n1384\t        a (::authority/authority opened)\n1385\t        open-journal (fn [dir]\n1386\t                       (let [b (open-file-backend! dir)\n1387\t                             j (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! b nil))]\n1388\t                         [b j]))\n1389\t        read-dir (fn [dir]\n1390\t                   (let [[b j] (open-journal dir)]\n1391\t                     (try (->data (journal-values j))\n1392\t                          (finally (file-journal/close! b)))))]\n1393\t    (try\n1394\t      {:status (:yin.k/status opened)\n1395\t       :projection (->data (when a (authority/projection a)))\n1396\t       :targets (into {}\n1397\t                      (map (fn [i]\n1398\t                             [(->data i) (if-some [r (when a (authority/target-reader a i))]\n1399\t                                           (->data (read-values r))\n1400\t                                           :absent)]))\n1401\t                      targets)\n1402\t       :outcomes (if a (->data (read-values (admission/outcome-reader a))) [])\n1403\t       :journals (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (read-dir (str (:journals p) \"/\" h \"-progress\"))]))\n1404\t                       holders)\n1405\t       :replies (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (read-dir (str (:journals p) \"/\" h \"-reply\"))]))\n1406\t                      holders)\n1407\t       :side (read-dir (:side p))}\n1408\t      (finally\n1409\t        (when a (authority/close! a))\n1410\t        (when backend (file-journal/close! backend))))))\n1411\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e817baf-a368-4767-b2d4-2b25a4b937e7","uuid":"8ef465bf-cb31-47cf-ad8a-e9048677f67c","timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:46:23.587Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_world.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-world\n  \"M-next stage E: the world one life of a crash/partition scenario runs\n   in, driven only through `yin.vm.ucf.compose` (linker-dht 14.2.4,\n   UCF 7.11.1 clause 10 and the composition halves of clauses 3 and 8).\n\n   A scenario is a sequence of lives over one root directory.  Every\n   piece of state a later life may read lives on durable file media\n   under that root -- the authority's ledger (a dao.stream.journal.file\n   backend), every holder's progress and reply journal\n   (`compose/file-journals`), the content store (a dao.jing.file\n   content file, the node's carrier for bodies and code) and the side\n   log of at-least-once external IO -- so a life is a fresh runtime:\n   nothing in memory crosses from one life to the next.  The program\n   and source streams are outside custody; each life rebuilds its own\n   instance of them under their fixed identities from the life's spec,\n   the way a receiver attaches a stream by its carried descriptor.\n\n   A life is plain data (`run-life`'s spec) and so is everything it\n   reports, so the same life runs in this process (the isolated-runtime\n   mode every lane has, Dart's only form) or inside a separate operating\n   system process (`yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer`, the JVM and Node process\n   transport) and its report is compared as data either way.\n\n   Kills.  Every durable medium is wrapped mortal: a named cut (the\n   `cuts` table) fires at one exact boundary -- before or after a given\n   journal frame, before or after a given content-store put, or after a\n   composition tick whose state matches -- and from then on the life is\n   dead.  Inside a peer process the cut prints its event and blocks\n   until the parent destroys the process (SIGKILL); in this process it\n   marks every medium dead (no further durable write happens) and\n   unwinds, and the runner releases the locks the dead runtime held --\n   the only thing an operating system does for a killed process.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.jing.file :as jing-file]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.journal :as journal]\n            [dao.stream.journal.file :as file-journal]\n            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n            #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n                       [\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]]\n                :clj [[clojure.java.io :as io]])\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.admission :as admission]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.compose :as compose]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint :as checkpoint]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Plain data\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- host-bytes?\n  [x]\n  #?(:clj (bytes? x)\n     :cljs (instance? js/Uint8Array x)\n     :cljd (instance? typed/Uint8List x)))\n\n\n(defn ->data\n  \"`x` as plain data every host prints and reads back the same: maps,\n   vectors, sets, scalars.  Host bytes become their blake3 digest\n   ({::bytes hex}), so two byte strings compare equal exactly when their\n   bytes are; anything else that is not data (a handle, a function, a\n   machine) becomes {::opaque true}.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)\n        (number? x) (uuid? x))\n    x\n\n    (host-bytes? x) {::bytes (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 x)}\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(->data k) (->data v)])) x)\n    (vector? x) (mapv ->data x)\n    (set? x) (into #{} (map ->data) x)\n    (sequential? x) (mapv ->data x)\n    :else {::opaque true}))\n\n\n(defn digest-of\n  \"The digest form ->data gives host bytes `bs`.\"\n  [bs]\n  {::bytes (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 bs)})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Scratch roots\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn temp-root\n  \"A fresh scratch root under target/.\"\n  []\n  (str \"target/stage-e-\" (random-uuid)))\n\n\n(defn cleanup-root!\n  [dir]\n  #?(:cljd (try (.deleteSync (dart-io/Directory. dir) .recursive true)\n                (catch Object _ nil))\n     :clj (letfn [(delete-recursively!\n                    [f]\n                    (when (.isDirectory f)\n                      (doseq [child (.listFiles f)]\n                        (delete-recursively! child)))\n                    (.delete f))]\n            (delete-recursively! (io/file dir)))\n     :cljs (try (.rmSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true :force true})\n                (catch :default _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn- ensure-dir!\n  [dir]\n  #?(:cljd (let [d (dart-io/Directory. dir)]\n             (when-not (.existsSync d) (.createSync d .recursive true)))\n     :clj (.mkdirs (io/file dir))\n     :cljs (.mkdirSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true})))\n\n\n(defn paths\n  \"The durable media of the world over `root`.\"\n  [root]\n  {:authority (str root \"/authority\")\n   :journals (str root \"/journals\")\n   :store (str root \"/store.jing\")\n   :side (str root \"/side\")})\n\n\n(defn destroy-authority!\n  \"Permanently lose the authority's state under `root`: its content file\n   is overwritten with bytes that are no content log, the way a lost\n   disk leaves it.  No reopen can recover a ledger from it.\"\n  [root]\n  (let [path (str (:authority (paths root)) \"/\" file-journal/content-name)]\n    #?(:cljd (.writeAsStringSync (dart-io/File. path) \"lost authority state\")\n       :clj (spit path \"lost authority state\")\n       :cljs (.writeFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path \"lost authority state\"))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The life context: events, counters, the cut and the kill\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn context\n  \"A life's context.  `emit!` takes each event map as it happens (a peer\n   prints it at once); `at-cut` is called when the life's cut fires: a\n   peer's never returns -- the parent kills the process inside it -- and\n   the in-process runner's returns so the life can unwind dead.\"\n  [{:keys [cut fail emit! at-cut]}]\n  {:cut cut\n   :fail fail\n   :failed (atom nil)\n   :emit! (or emit! (fn [_]))\n   :at-cut (or at-cut (fn []))\n   :dead (atom false)\n   :fired (atom nil)\n   :hits (atom {})\n   :attaches (atom 0)\n   :observes (atom 0)\n   :opened (atom [])})\n\n\n(defn killed?\n  [e]\n  (true? (::killed (ex-data e))))\n\n\n(defn- dead-throw!\n  []\n  (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a dead runtime wrote nothing\" {::killed true})))\n\n\n(defn- fire!\n  [ctx at]\n  (reset! (:fired ctx) at)\n  (reset! (:dead ctx) true)\n  ((:emit! ctx) {:event :cut :cut (:cut ctx) :at at})\n  ((:at-cut ctx))\n  (throw (ex-info \"stage E: killed at a cut\" {::killed true :cut (:cut ctx)})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The named cuts\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- record-is\n  [journal-kind action]\n  (fn [r]\n    (and (= journal-kind (:yin.k/journal r))\n         (or (nil? action) (= action (:yin.k/action r))))))\n\n\n(defn- projection-of\n  [c]\n  (when-some [a (:authority c)]\n    (authority/projection a)))\n\n\n(defn- journal-records-of\n  \"Holder `h`'s whole progress journal, read through a fresh open of its\n   backend (the restart's view).\"\n  [c h]\n  (let [backend (get-in c [:progress h :backend])\n        j (if (some? backend)\n            (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! backend nil))\n            (compose/journal-of c h))]\n    (if (nil? j)\n      []\n      (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor j :dao.stream/oldest))\n             records []]\n        (let [answer (stream/next j cursor)]\n          (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n            (recur (:dao.stream/cursor answer) (conj records (:dao.stream/value answer)))\n            records))))))\n\n\n(defn- holder-records-match?\n  [c h pred]\n  (boolean (some pred (journal-records-of c h))))\n\n\n(defn- exit-occurrence\n  [c h]\n  (get-in c [:holders h :exit :occurrence]))\n\n\n(defn- read-values\n  [h]\n  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n         values []]\n    (let [r (stream/next h cursor)]\n      (if (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)) (< (count values) 1000))\n        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj values (:dao.stream/value r)))\n        values))))\n\n\n(defn inbound-of\n  \"The requests of `kind` (every request when nil) that reached holder\n   `h`'s inbound in this life, in stream order.\"\n  [c h kind]\n  (if-some [inbound (get-in c [:inbounds h])]\n    (filterv #(or (nil? kind) (= kind (:yin.k/request %))) (read-values inbound))\n    []))\n\n\n(defn- admission-commit?\n  \"Whether ledger record `r` is the transaction that commits an admitted\n   effect: one of its datoms is the :yin.k/admitted custody fact.\"\n  [r]\n  (boolean (some (fn [d]\n                   (and (sequential? d)\n                        (= :yin.k/custody (nth d 1 nil))\n                        (= :yin.k/admitted (nth d 2 nil))))\n                 (get-in r [:dao.space/transaction :datoms]))))\n\n\n(def cuts\n  \"Every named cut a scenario may ask for: where it fires and when.\n   :site is a journal ([:progress h] or [:reply h]), :authority, :store\n   or :tick; :when is :before or :after the matched write (a tick cut\n   fires after the tick whose composition matches); :match is a\n   predicate over the decoded journal record, the put ({:address a}) or\n   the composition; :nth counts matches (default 1).\"\n  {;; ---- row 7: completion\n   :row7/after-successor-append\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (let [s (exit-occurrence c \"h1\")]\n               (and (some? s)\n                    (holder-records-match?\n                      c \"h1\" #(and ((record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/offer) %)\n                                   (= s (:yin.k/occurrence %)))))))}\n   :row7/after-resumed-report\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (let [l (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :lease])]\n               (and (some? l)\n                    (some? (get-in (projection-of c) [:leases l :yin.k/result])))))}\n   :row7/after-release-append\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (holder-records-match?\n               c \"h1\" #(and ((record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/release) %)\n                            (= :dao.stream/ok (:yin.k/append %)))))}\n   :row7/after-closure\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (let [o (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :occurrence])]\n               (and (some? o)\n                    (some? (get-in (projection-of c) [:occurrences o :yin.k/closed])))))}\n   :row7/while-running\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c] (= :running (get-in c [:holders \"h1\" :phase])))}\n\n   ;; ---- row 4 and clause 8: around the atomic effect commitment (the\n   ;; ledger transaction that records the admitted effect)\n   :row4/before-commit\n   {:site :authority :when :before :match admission-commit?}\n   :row4/after-commit\n   {:site :authority :when :after :match admission-commit?}\n   :row4/before-result-append\n   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :before\n    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/admit (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n   :row4/admit-uncarried\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/admit)))}\n\n   ;; ---- row 5: the input record\n   :row5/input-uncarried\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/input)))}\n   :row5/input-carried\n   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :after\n    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/input (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n\n   ;; ---- row 2 and the D14 journal brackets: the export's phases\n   :export/after-minted\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/minted nil)}\n   :export/after-serve-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/serve)}\n   :export/after-serve-ack\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/serve)}\n   :export/after-store-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/store)}\n   :export/store-put-before\n   {:site :store :when :before :match (fn [_] true)}\n   :export/store-put-after\n   {:site :store :when :after :match (fn [_] true)}\n   :export/after-store-ack\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/store)}\n   :export/before-fenced\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/fenced nil)}\n   :export/after-fenced\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/fenced nil)}\n   :export/after-offer-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/offer)}\n   :export/after-offer-attempt\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/offer)}\n   :export/after-offer-ack\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/offer)}\n\n   ;; ---- the inbox retention machine (D15a) and the grant bracket\n   :inbox/before-retention\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/inbox nil)}\n   :inbox/after-retention\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/inbox nil)}\n   :journal/before-proposal-attempt\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :before :match (record-is :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/proposal)}\n   :journal/after-proposal-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/proposal)}\n   :journal/after-grant-ack\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/ack :yin.k/grant)}\n   :journal/after-resumed-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/resumed)}\n   :journal/after-release-intent\n   {:site [:progress \"h1\"] :when :after :match (record-is :yin.k/intent :yin.k/release)}\n\n   ;; ---- clause 8: after the first commit's reply stands\n   :clause8/committed\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c]\n             (some #(and (= :yin.k/admit (:yin.k/reply %))\n                         (= :committed (get-in % [:yin.k/answer :yin.k/admission])))\n                   (if-some [j (get-in c [:reply-journals \"h1\" :journal])]\n                     (read-values j)\n                     [])))}\n\n   ;; ---- row 6: a lost reply (the process dies before the front's\n   ;; append of the proposal's reply)\n   :row6/proposal-reply-lost\n   {:site [:reply \"h1\"] :when :before\n    :match (fn [r] (= :yin.k/proposal (:yin.k/reply r)))}\n\n   ;; ---- the freeze's second stored object (the body)\n   :export/body-put-before\n   {:site :store :when :before :match (fn [_] true) :nth 2}\n   :export/body-put-after\n   {:site :store :when :after :match (fn [_] true) :nth 2}\n\n   ;; ---- clause 3: between assign and discharge\n   :seq/after-assign\n   {:site :tick\n    :match (fn [c] (seq (inbound-of c \"h1\" :yin.k/admit)))}})\n\n\n(defn- cut-spec\n  [ctx]\n  (when-some [k (:cut ctx)]\n    (or (get cuts k)\n        (throw (ex-info \"stage E: unknown cut\" {:cut k})))))\n\n\n(defn- hit!\n  \"Whether the life's cut matches this write at `site` (counted against\n   :nth), answering :before, :after or nil.\"\n  [ctx site subject]\n  (let [spec (cut-spec ctx)]\n    (when (and (some? spec)\n               (nil? @(:fired ctx))\n               (= site (:site spec))\n               ((:match spec) subject))\n      (let [n (get (swap! (:hits ctx) update site (fnil inc 0)) site)]\n        (when (= n (or (:nth spec) 1))\n          (or (:when spec) :after))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Mortal media\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- frame-record\n  [bs]\n  (try\n    (::journal/value (cbor/decode bs))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n\n\n(defn- fail-hit!\n  \"Whether the life's uncertain-append failure ({:like cut-name\n   :persist? bool}) matches this write at `site`: the first match only.\"\n  [ctx site subject]\n  (when-some [{:keys [like]} (:fail ctx)]\n    (let [spec (get cuts like)]\n      (when (and (nil? @(:failed ctx))\n                 (= site (:site spec))\n                 ((:match spec) subject))\n        (reset! (:failed ctx) {:site site :like like})\n        true))))\n\n\n(defn mortal-backend\n  \"Journal backend `b` at `site`, mortal under `ctx`: once the life is\n   dead every frame write throws having written nothing, and the life's\n   cut, when it names this site, fires before or after its frame.\"\n  [ctx site b]\n  (swap! (:opened ctx) conj [:backend b])\n  (let [write! (::journal/write-frame! b)\n        truncate! (::journal/truncate! b)]\n    (assoc b\n           ::journal/write-frame!\n           (fn [bs]\n             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n             (when (fail-hit! ctx site (frame-record bs))\n               ;; an uncertain append: the frame lands or not, and the\n               ;; writer is answered a throw either way -- the process\n               ;; lives on, its journal's answer unknown\n               (when (:persist? (:fail ctx)) (write! bs))\n               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :uncertain :site site\n                              :persisted? (boolean (:persist? (:fail ctx)))\n                              :record (->data (frame-record bs))})\n               (throw (ex-info \"stage E: an uncertain append\" {::uncertain true})))\n             (let [hit (hit! ctx site (frame-record bs))]\n               (when (= :before hit)\n                 (fire! ctx {:site site :when :before\n                             :record (->data (frame-record bs))}))\n               (let [r (write! bs)]\n                 (when (= :after hit)\n                   (fire! ctx {:site site :when :after\n                               :record (->data (frame-record bs))}))\n                 r)))\n           ::journal/truncate!\n           (fn [n]\n             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n             (truncate! n)))))\n\n\n(defn mortal-store\n  \"Content store `base`, mortal under `ctx`, its puts cut at :store; its\n   gets answer the default for every address in `unreadable` (an\n   accepted checkpoint whose bytes cannot be read).\"\n  [ctx base unreadable]\n  (swap! (:opened ctx) conj [:store base])\n  (let [put! (:put-bytes-fn base)\n        get! (:get-bytes-fn base)]\n    (assoc base\n           :put-bytes-fn\n           (fn [address bs]\n             (when @(:dead ctx) (dead-throw!))\n             (let [hit (hit! ctx :store {:address address})]\n               (when (= :before hit)\n                 (fire! ctx {:site :store :when :before :address address}))\n               (let [r (put! address bs)]\n                 (when (= :after hit)\n                   (fire! ctx {:site :store :when :after :address address}))\n                 r)))\n           :get-bytes-fn\n           (fn\n             ([address] (get! address))\n             ([address default]\n              (if (contains? unreadable address)\n                default\n                (get! address default)))))))\n\n\n(defn- open-file-backend!\n  [dir]\n  (ensure-dir! dir)\n  (let [r (file-journal/backend! dir)]\n    (or (::file-journal/backend r)\n        (throw (ex-info \"stage E: a durable journal directory refused\"\n                        {:dir dir :answer r})))))\n\n\n(defn- mortal-journals\n  \"compose/file-journals over `root`, every backend it opens mortal at\n   [:progress h] or [:reply h].\"\n  [ctx root]\n  (let [base (compose/file-journals root)]\n    (assoc base\n           :progress-backend!\n           (fn [h] (mortal-backend ctx [:progress h] ((:progress-backend! base) h)))\n           :reply-backend!\n           (fn [h] (mortal-backend ctx [:reply h] ((:reply-backend! base) h))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Streams outside custody\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn scenario-stream\n  \"A stream outside custody, rebuilt by every life under its fixed\n   `identity`: `values` at integer positions from zero, positions below\n   `floor` evicted (their reads answer gap with the floor as the\n   successor cursor).  Integer positions make a position lifted from one\n   life's instance a valid cursor on the next life's.\"\n  [identity values floor]\n  (let [vs (atom (vec values))]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor floor})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (let [values @vs]\n          (cond\n            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count values))))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n            (< cursor floor)\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/cursor floor}\n            (< cursor (count values))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n             :dao.stream/value (nth values cursor)\n             :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n            :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (swap! vs conj x)\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n\n\n(defn journal-stream\n  \"A durable stream over journal handle `j` under the fixed `identity`:\n   integer positions over the journal's own, so every life reads the\n   whole history any life appended -- the side log of at-least-once\n   external IO.\"\n  [identity j]\n  (let [jid (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor j))]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (if-not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor))\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n          (let [r (stream/next j {:dao.stream.memory-log/identity jid\n                                  :dao.stream.memory-log/position cursor})]\n            (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n              :dao.stream/ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n                              :dao.stream/value (:dao.stream/value r)\n                              :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (stream/append! j x)))))\n\n\n(defn- answering-inbound\n  \"A log-shaped inbound whose appends answer `@outcome`: :dao.stream/ok\n   lands the request; any other outcome lands nothing (the carrier full,\n   refusing, or failing under the send).\"\n  [identity outcome]\n  (let [values (atom [])]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (let [vs @values]\n          (cond\n            (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n            (< cursor (count vs))\n            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n             :dao.stream/value (nth vs cursor)\n             :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n            :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (let [o @outcome]\n          (when (= :dao.stream/ok o) (swap! values conj x))\n          {:dao.stream/outcome o})))))\n\n\n(defn- held-inbound\n  \"A log-shaped inbound whose reads answer :blocked while `held` (an\n   atom) is truthy: the holder's requests land, but the authority's\n   front cannot read them -- the holder partitioned from its\n   authority.  Healed, the front reads every request that landed.\"\n  [identity held]\n  (let [values (atom [])]\n    (reify\n      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n      (descriptor\n        [_]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n         :dao.stream/identity identity\n         :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                 :dao.stream/identity identity}})\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n\n      (cursor\n        [_ _anchor]\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n      (next\n        [_ cursor]\n        (if @held\n          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}\n          (let [vs @values]\n            (cond\n              (not (and (integer? cursor) (<= 0 cursor (count vs))))\n              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n              (< cursor (count vs))\n              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n               :dao.stream/value (nth vs cursor)\n               :dao.stream/cursor (inc cursor)}\n              :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n\n\n      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n      (append!\n        [_ x]\n        (swap! values conj x)\n        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n\n\n(defn- log-writer\n  []\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Machines and holder seams\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(def prog-id \"prog-c\")\n(def source-id \"src-s\")\n(def side-id \"side-x\")\n\n\n(defn- parked-reader-over\n  \"A real gated machine over `source`, parked on its first read: one\n   more delivered value and it halts with :done.\"\n  [source]\n  (let [m0 (s/load-ast (s/new-machine)\n                       (s/then {:type :stream/next, :source (s/v 'c)}\n                               (s/lit :done)))\n        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n        [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)]\n    (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'c cref} :yin.k/gate :running))))\n\n\n(defn- reading-writer\n  \"A real gated machine over `source`, parked on its first read: the\n   value it reads is written to the enrolled `target`, then :side to\n   `side`, then it halts with :done.\"\n  [source target side]\n  (let [m0 (s/load-ast (s/new-machine)\n                       (s/let1 'v (s/next-of (s/v 'c))\n                               (s/then {:type :stream/put, :target (s/v 'w),\n                                        :val (s/v 'v)}\n                                       (s/then {:type :stream/put,\n                                                :target (s/v 'x),\n                                                :val (s/lit :side)}\n                                               (s/lit :done)))))\n        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n        [cref m2] (engine/handle-cursor m1 {:stream sref} :k1)\n        [wref m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 target)\n        [xref m4] (engine/attach-resource m3 side)]\n    (vm/run (assoc m4 :store {'c cref, 'w wref, 'x xref}\n                   :yin.k/gate :running))))\n\n\n(defn- attach-over\n  [ctx table]\n  (fn [descriptor]\n    (swap! (:attaches ctx) inc)\n    (if-some [h (get table (:dao.stream/identity descriptor))]\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/handle h}\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found})))\n\n\n(defn- observe-over\n  [ctx]\n  (fn [h op arg]\n    (swap! (:observes ctx) inc)\n    (case op\n      :next (stream/next h arg)\n      :cursor (stream/cursor h arg))))\n\n\n(defn- same-id-server\n  []\n  (fn [h]\n    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor h))]\n      {:dao.stream/identity id\n       :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                            :dao.stream/identity id}})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Opening a life's world\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- composition-config\n  [w mode]\n  (cond-> {:mode mode\n           :source-index (fn [] @s/source-index)\n           :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n           :store (:store w)\n           :diagnostics (:diagnostics w)\n           :medium \"stage-e\"\n           :clock (fn [] {:s @(:clock w)})}\n    (= :exclusive mode) (assoc :failure-model :process-crash\n                               :backend (:authority-backend w)\n                               :duration {:s 30}\n                               :journals (:journals w))))\n\n\n(defn- world-table\n  \"The holder table and protection of the life's world kind.\"\n  [w]\n  (case (:kind w)\n    :parked {:table (if (= :none (:attach w)) {} {prog-id (:prog w)})\n             :protection {prog-id :at-least-once}}\n    :rows {:table (cond-> {source-id (:source w) side-id (:side w)}\n                    (:target w) (assoc (:target w) (:reader w)))\n           :protection (cond-> {source-id :at-least-once side-id :at-least-once}\n                         (:target w) (assoc (:target w) :enrolled))}))\n\n\n(defn- holder-seams\n  [ctx w]\n  (let [{:keys [table protection]} (world-table w)]\n    {:protection protection\n     :receiver (s/new-machine)\n     :attach! (attach-over ctx table)\n     :observe! (observe-over ctx)\n     :serve! (if (= :parked (:kind w))\n               (fn [_h]\n                 {:dao.stream/identity prog-id\n                  :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n                                       :dao.stream/identity prog-id}})\n               (same-id-server))}))\n\n\n(defn- source-machine\n  [w]\n  (case (:kind w)\n    :parked (parked-reader-over (scenario-stream prog-id [] 0))\n    :rows (reading-writer (:source w) (:reader w) (:side w))))\n\n\n(defn open-world!\n  \"Open the life's world over `spec`: the durable media, mortal under\n   `ctx`, and the composition over them.  Answers the world map with\n   :c the open composition, or :refusal the composition's data refusal.\"\n  [ctx spec]\n  (let [{:keys [root kind mode]} spec\n        mode (or mode :exclusive)\n        p (paths root)\n        _ (ensure-dir! root)\n        partitioned (atom false)\n        authority-backend (when (= :exclusive mode)\n                            (let [b (mortal-backend ctx :authority\n                                                    (open-file-backend! (:authority p)))\n                                  write! (::journal/write-frame! b)]\n                              ;; the protected consumer partitioned from\n                              ;; its authority: every frame write fails\n                              ;; while the flag stands\n                              (assoc b ::journal/write-frame!\n                                     (fn [bs]\n                                       (if @partitioned\n                                         (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the authority is partitioned\" {}))\n                                         (write! bs))))))\n        store (mortal-store ctx (jing-file/create-content-file (:store p))\n                            (set (:unreadable spec)))\n        side-backend (when (= :rows kind)\n                       (mortal-backend ctx :side (open-file-backend! (:side p))))\n        side (when side-backend\n               (journal-stream side-id (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! side-backend nil))))\n        w {:root root\n           :kind kind\n           :mode mode\n           :attach (:attach spec)\n           :clock (atom (or (:clock spec) 1))\n           :store store\n           :diagnostics (log-writer)\n           :authority-backend authority-backend\n           :side-backend side-backend\n           :journals (if (= :exclusive mode)\n                       (mortal-journals ctx (:journals p))\n                       (compose/memory-journals (atom {})))\n           :prog (scenario-stream prog-id (or (:prog spec) []) 0)\n           :source (scenario-stream source-id (or (:source spec) [\"A\"])\n                                    (or (:evict-floor spec) 0))\n           :side side\n           :partitioned partitioned\n           :carrier (atom :dao.stream/ok)\n           :held (atom false)\n           :inbound (:inbound spec)}\n        opened (compose/open! (composition-config w mode))\n        c (:yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition opened)]\n    (if (nil? c)\n      (assoc w :refusal (->data opened))\n      (let [w (assoc w :c c)]\n        (if (= :rows kind)\n          (let [i (or (:target spec)\n                      (let [e (compose/enroll! c)]\n                        ((:emit! ctx) {:event :enrolled :target (:yin.k/target e)})\n                        (:yin.k/target e)))]\n            (assoc w :target i :reader (compose/target-reader c i)))\n          w)))))\n\n\n(defn release-dead!\n  \"What the operating system does for a killed process, done for a life\n   killed in this process: every file backend and the store it opened\n   released, nothing written.\"\n  [ctx]\n  (doseq [[kind x] @(:opened ctx)]\n    (try\n      (case kind\n        :backend (when (contains? x ::file-journal/close!) (file-journal/close! x))\n        :store ((:close-fn x)))\n      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn close-world!\n  \"Release everything a live world holds: the composition (its journal\n   backends), the authority backend, the side log and the store.\"\n  [w]\n  (let [safe (fn [f]\n               (try (f) (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))]\n    (when-some [c (:c w)] (safe #(compose/close! c)))\n    (when-some [b (:authority-backend w)] (safe #(file-journal/close! b)))\n    (when-some [b (:side-backend w)] (safe #(file-journal/close! b)))\n    (when-some [close! (get-in w [:store :close-fn])] (safe close!))\n    nil))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Reading a live world\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- journal-values\n  [j]\n  (if (nil? j)\n    []\n    (read-values j)))\n\n\n(defn replies-of\n  \"Every reply the composition's front wrote into holder `h`'s reply\n   journal (both tenures': the journal is durable).\"\n  [c h]\n  (journal-values (get-in c [:reply-journals h :journal])))\n\n\n(defn holder-summary\n  [st]\n  (->data (merge (select-keys st [:phase :status :detail :occurrence :lease])\n                 {:epoch (get-in st [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch])\n                  :next-op-seq (get-in st [:machine :yin.k/custody :yin.k/next-op-seq])\n                  :stopped? (:stopped? st)\n                  :machine? (some? (:machine st))})))\n\n\n(defn snapshot\n  \"Everything a check may read of the live world, as data.\"\n  [ctx w]\n  (let [c (:c w)\n        hs (sort (keys (:holders c)))]\n    {:holders (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (holder-summary (get-in c [:holders h]))])) hs)\n     :policy (:yin.k/policy c)\n     :projection (->data (projection-of c))\n     :journals (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (journal-records-of c h))])) hs)\n     :replies (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (replies-of c h))])) hs)\n     :inbound (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (inbound-of c h nil))])) hs)\n     :targets (if-some [i (:target w)]\n                {:target (->data i)\n                 :values (->data (read-values (compose/target-reader c i)))}\n                {})\n     :outcomes (if-some [r (compose/outcome-reader c)]\n                 (->data (read-values r))\n                 [])\n     :side (if-some [side (:side w)] (->data (read-values side)) [])\n     :fences (into {}\n                   (keep (fn [r]\n                           (when (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n                             (let [a (:yin.k/address r)\n                                   bs ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) a nil)]\n                               [a (when bs (digest-of bs))]))))\n                   (mapcat #(journal-records-of c %) hs))\n     :packs (into {}\n                  (keep (fn [r]\n                          (when (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n                            (let [a (:yin.k/address r)\n                                  bs ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) a nil)]\n                              (when bs\n                                (let [wire (cbor/decode bs)]\n                                  [a {:root (:yin.k/root wire)\n                                      :baseline (checkpoint/inspect a bs)\n                                      :sorted? (= (mapv first (:yin.k/rows wire))\n                                                  (vec (sort (map first (:yin.k/rows wire)))))\n                                      :canonical-bytes (digest-of (cbor/encode (rows/emit (rows/decode wire))))}]))))))\n                  (mapcat #(journal-records-of c %) hs))\n     :diagnostics (->data (read-values (:diagnostics w)))\n     :arbitration (->data (compose/arbitration c))\n     :counts {:attaches @(:attaches ctx) :observes @(:observes ctx)}\n     :clock @(:clock w)}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The life's program: plain-data operations over the composition\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- durable-records\n  \"Holder `h`'s progress journal: through the composition when this life\n   composes `h`, else read from its durable directory (a holder a\n   previous life ran).\"\n  [w h]\n  (if (contains? (get-in w [:c :holders]) h)\n    (journal-records-of (:c w) h)\n    (let [b (open-file-backend! (str (:journals (paths (:root w))) \"/\" h \"-progress\"))]\n      (try\n        (journal-values (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! b nil)))\n        (finally (file-journal/close! b))))))\n\n\n(defn- checkpoint-from\n  \"The checkpoint a candidate is added over, read from the durable\n   journal of `of` and the store: :fence the source's export, :successor\n   the exit's successor, or an explicit {:address a}.\"\n  [w {:keys [kind of address]}]\n  (let [records (durable-records w of)\n        fence (fn [o]\n                (some (fn [r]\n                        (when (and (= :yin.k/fenced (:yin.k/journal r))\n                                   (or (nil? o) (= o (:yin.k/occurrence r))))\n                          r))\n                      records))\n        address (case kind\n                  :fence (:yin.k/address (fence nil))\n                  :successor (let [mint (last (filter\n                                                (fn [r]\n                                                  (and (= :yin.k/minted (:yin.k/journal r))\n                                                       (= :yin.k/successor (:yin.k/role r))))\n                                                records))]\n                               (:yin.k/address (fence (:yin.k/occurrence mint))))\n                  :variant (:address (:variant w))\n                  :address address)\n        bs (when address ((:get-bytes-fn (:store w)) address nil))]\n    (when (nil? bs)\n      (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the checkpoint is absent from the store\"\n                      {:checkpoint {:kind kind :of of :address (->data address)}})))\n    {:address address :bytes bs}))\n\n\n(defn- inbound-for\n  \"Holder `h`'s inbound, when the life's spec names one: :answering, a\n   carrier whose appends answer the life's carrier outcome; :held, a\n   stream the front cannot read while the life holds the partition.\"\n  [w h]\n  (case (get (:inbound w) h)\n    :answering {:inbound (answering-inbound (str \"inbound-\" h) (:carrier w))}\n    :held {:inbound (held-inbound (str \"inbound-\" h) (:held w))}\n    nil))\n\n\n(defn- offer-variant!\n  \"A second encoding of the occurrence holder `h` fenced: the same root\n   with reversed rows in different canonical bytes, put in the store\n   and offered through `h`'s own inbound.  Answers {:address :bytes}.\"\n  [w h]\n  (let [{:keys [address bytes]} (checkpoint-from w {:kind :fence :of h})\n        body (cbor/decode bytes)\n        o (:yin.k/occurrence (checkpoint/inspect address bytes))\n        v-bytes (cbor/encode (update body :yin.k/rows #(vec (reverse %))))\n        v-address (rows/pack-address (cbor/decode v-bytes))]\n    ((:put-bytes-fn (:store w)) v-address v-bytes)\n    (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h])\n                    {:yin.k/request :yin.k/offer\n                     :yin.k/request-id [:stage-e/variant (str address)]\n                     :yin.k/id v-address\n                     :yin.k/bytes v-bytes\n                     :yin.k/medium \"stage-e\"})\n    {:address v-address :bytes v-bytes :occurrence o}))\n\n\n(defn- holder-config\n  [ctx w extra]\n  (merge (holder-seams ctx w) extra))\n\n\n(defn- add-source\n  [ctx w h]\n  (update w :c compose/source h (holder-config ctx w (merge {:machine (source-machine w)}\n                                                            (inbound-for w h)))))\n\n\n(defn- add-candidate\n  [ctx w h checkpoint opts]\n  (let [{:keys [address bytes]} (checkpoint-from w checkpoint)\n        seams (holder-config ctx w (merge {:bytes bytes :address address}\n                                          (inbound-for w h)))\n        seams (if (= :none (:attach opts))\n                (assoc seams :attach! (fn [_] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/not-found}))\n                seams)]\n    (update w :c compose/holder h seams)))\n\n\n(defn- dead?\n  [ctx]\n  @(:dead ctx))\n\n\n(defn- tick!\n  \"One tick of `f` over the world's composition; the life's tick cut is\n   checked after it.  A dead life ends here.\"\n  [ctx w f]\n  (let [c' (f (:c w))\n        w (assoc w :c c')]\n    (when (dead? ctx) (dead-throw!))\n    (let [spec (cut-spec ctx)]\n      (when (and (some? spec) (= :tick (:site spec)) (nil? @(:fired ctx))\n                 ((:match spec) c'))\n        (fire! ctx {:site :tick\n                    :holders (into {} (map (fn [[h st]] [h (holder-summary st)])) (:holders c'))\n                    :inbound (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (->data (inbound-of c' h nil))]))\n                                   (keys (:holders c')))})))\n    w))\n\n\n(def ^:private planes\n  {:step compose/step\n   :control compose/control-step\n   :program compose/program-step})\n\n\n(defn- phase?\n  [w h phase]\n  (= phase (get-in w [:c :holders h :phase])))\n\n\n(defn- until\n  \"Ticks of `plane` until `pred` holds of the world or `n` are spent;\n   answers [world held?].\"\n  [ctx w plane pred n]\n  (loop [w w k 0]\n    (if (pred w)\n      [w true]\n      (if (>= k n)\n        [w false]\n        (recur (tick! ctx w (get planes plane)) (inc k))))))\n\n\n(defn- admit-request\n  [rid target envelope]\n  {:yin.k/request :yin.k/admit\n   :yin.k/request-id rid\n   :yin.k/target target\n   :yin.k/fenced-envelope envelope})\n\n\n(defn- envelope\n  [lease epoch op-id value]\n  {:yin.k/envelope :yin.k/fenced-v1\n   :yin.k/incarnation lease\n   :yin.k/epoch epoch\n   :yin.k/op-id op-id\n   :yin.k/value value})\n\n\n(defn- holder-binding\n  [w h]\n  (let [st (get-in w [:c :holders h])]\n    {:lease (:lease st)\n     :epoch (get-in st [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch])\n     :occurrence (:occurrence st)}))\n\n\n(defn- resolve-arg\n  \"Operation arguments may name a holder's live binding: [:binding h k].\"\n  [w x]\n  (if (and (vector? x) (= :binding (first x)))\n    (get (holder-binding w (nth x 1)) (nth x 2))\n    x))\n\n\n(defn- admit!\n  \"Append an authored admit to holder `h`'s inbound and run control ticks\n   until its reply lands (or `n` are spent).\"\n  [ctx w h {:keys [rid target lease epoch op-id value await?]}]\n  (let [target (cond (= :other target) (:other w)\n                     (some? target) (resolve-arg w target)\n                     :else (:target w))\n        lease (resolve-arg w lease)\n        epoch (resolve-arg w epoch)\n        op-id (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (resolve-arg w v)])) op-id)\n        n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n    (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h])\n                    (admit-request rid target (envelope lease epoch op-id value)))\n    (if (false? await?)\n      (tick! ctx w compose/control-step)\n      (first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)))))\n\n\n(defn- run-op\n  \"One operation of a life's program; answers [world report-additions].\"\n  [ctx w [op & args]]\n  (case op\n    :source [(add-source ctx w (first args)) nil]\n    :candidate (let [[h checkpoint opts] args]\n                 [(add-candidate ctx w h checkpoint opts) nil])\n    :until (let [[h phase n plane] args\n                 [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step) #(phase? % h phase) n)]\n             [w {:until [[h phase held?]]}])\n    :until-status (let [[h status n] args\n                        [w held?] (until ctx w :step\n                                         #(= status (get-in % [:c :holders h :status])) n)]\n                    [w {:until [[h status held?]]}])\n    :until-inbound (let [[h kind n plane] args\n                         [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n                                          #(seq (inbound-of (:c %) h kind)) n)]\n                     [w {:until [[h kind held?]]}])\n    :until-reply (let [[h kind n plane] args\n                       [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n                                        #(some (fn [r] (= kind (:yin.k/reply r)))\n                                               (replies-of (:c %) h))\n                                        n)]\n                   [w {:until [[h kind held?]]}])\n    :until-some (let [[phase n] args\n                      [w held?] (until ctx w :step\n                                       (fn [w]\n                                         (some #(= phase (:phase %))\n                                               (vals (get-in w [:c :holders]))))\n                                       n)]\n                  [w {:until [[:some phase held?]]}])\n    :until-journal (let [[h kind action n plane] args\n                         [w held?] (until ctx w (or plane :step)\n                                          #(holder-records-match?\n                                             (:c %) h (record-is kind action))\n                                          n)]\n                     [w {:until [[h kind action held?]]}])\n    :ticks (let [[n plane] args]\n             [(reduce (fn [w _] (tick! ctx w (get planes (or plane :step)))) w (range n)) nil])\n    :hand-off [(update w :c compose/hand-off (first args)) nil]\n    :abort [(update w :c compose/abort (first args)) nil]\n    :clock (do (reset! (:clock w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :append-prog (do (stream/append! (:prog w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :admit (let [[h req] args] [(admit! ctx w h req) nil])\n    :enroll-other (let [e (compose/enroll! (:c w))]\n                    [(assoc w :other (:yin.k/target e)) {:other (->data (:yin.k/target e))}])\n    :snapshot (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n                ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key (first args) :snapshot snap})\n                [w {:snapshots {(first args) snap}}])\n    :binding (let [b (->data (holder-binding w (first args)))]\n               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :binding :holder (first args) :binding b})\n               [w {:bindings {(first args) b}}])\n    :inject (let [[h request] args\n                  n (count (replies-of (:c w) h))]\n              (stream/append! (get-in w [:c :inbounds h]) request)\n              [(first (until ctx w :control #(> (count (replies-of (:c %) h)) n) 20)) nil])\n    :offer-variant (let [[h] args\n                         v (offer-variant! w h)]\n                     ((:emit! ctx) {:event :variant :address (:address v)})\n                     [(assoc w :variant v) {:variant (->data (:address v))\n                                            :variant-baseline (checkpoint/inspect (:address v) (:bytes v))}])\n    :carrier (do (reset! (:carrier w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :hold (do (reset! (:held w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :partition-authority (do (reset! (:partitioned w) (first args)) [w nil])\n    :die (fire! ctx {:site :explicit :at (first args)})\n    :at-open (let [snap (snapshot ctx w)]\n               ((:emit! ctx) {:event :snapshot :key :at-open :snapshot snap})\n               [w {:at-open snap}])))\n\n\n(defn- merge-report\n  [report additions]\n  (merge-with (fn [a b] (if (and (map? a) (map? b)) (merge a b) (into a b)))\n              report additions))\n\n\n(defn- fork-row\n  \"A fork per host: fork runs when selected and is labelled fork, and an\n   exclusive requirement over a memory authority is refused, never\n   downgraded.\"\n  [ctx spec]\n  (let [refused (compose/open! {:source-index (fn [] @s/source-index)\n                                :mode :exclusive\n                                :failure-model :process-crash\n                                :backend (journal/memory-backend (atom []) nil)\n                                :duration {:s 30}\n                                :renewal-interval {:s 10}\n                                :store (jing-file/create-content-file\n                                         (str (:root spec) \"/refused.jing\"))\n                                :diagnostics (log-writer)\n                                :medium \"stage-e\"\n                                :clock (fn [] {:s 1})\n                                :journals (compose/file-journals\n                                            (str (:root spec) \"/refused\"))})\n        w (open-world! ctx (assoc spec :mode :fork :kind :parked))]\n    (try\n      (let [w (add-source ctx w \"h1\")\n            [w held?] (until ctx w :step #(phase? % \"h1\" :lifted) 12)]\n        {:refused (->data (dissoc refused :yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition))\n         :refused-composed? (some? (:yin.vm.ucf.compose/composition refused))\n         :fork {:held? held?\n                :policy (:yin.k/policy (:c w))\n                :status-policy (:yin.k/policy (compose/status (:c w)))\n                :arbitration (->data (compose/arbitration (:c w)))\n                :holder (holder-summary (get-in w [:c :holders \"h1\"]))\n                :address (->data (get-in w [:c :holders \"h1\" :detail :yin.k/address]))\n                :journal (->data (journal-records-of (:c w) \"h1\"))\n                :offers (->data (inbound-of (:c w) \"h1\" :yin.k/offer))\n                :fronts (count (:fronts (:c w)))\n                :outcome-reader? (some? (compose/outcome-reader (:c w)))}})\n      (finally (close-world! w)))))\n\n\n(defn run-life\n  \"Run one life of `spec` under `ctx` and answer its report (plain data).\n\n   spec:\n     :root     the scenario root (the durable media)\n     :kind     :parked (the parked-reader source of rows 1, 2, 6, 7) or\n               :rows (the reading-writer source over an enrolled target\n               of rows 3, 4, 5, 8)\n     :target   the enrolled target a :rows life reuses (absent: enroll,\n               emitting {:event :enrolled})\n     :clock    the life's starting clock reading, in seconds\n     :prog     the program stream's values this life sees\n     :source   the source stream's values; :evict-floor its eviction\n     :unreadable addresses the store cannot read\n     :attach   :none for an attach table that holds nothing\n     :ops      the life's program, a vector of operations (run-op)\n     :lose-authority true to destroy the authority's state first\n     :fork-row true for the per-host fork row instead\n\n   The cut, when any, is the context's.  A dead life throws ::killed\n   out of here; the caller (peer or in-process runner) decides what a\n   kill means.\"\n  [ctx spec]\n  (when (:lose-authority spec)\n    (destroy-authority! (:root spec)))\n  (cond\n    (:fork-row spec)\n    (fork-row ctx spec)\n\n    ;; a lost ledger the durable backend itself refuses to open never\n    ;; reaches the composition: fail stop, reported as data\n    (and (:lose-authority spec)\n         (not= :dao.stream/ok\n               (:dao.stream/outcome\n                 (let [r (file-journal/backend! (:authority (paths (:root spec))))]\n                   (when-some [b (::file-journal/backend r)] (file-journal/close! b))\n                   r))))\n    {:refusal {:stage :authority-backend\n               :answer (->data (file-journal/backend! (:authority (paths (:root spec)))))}}\n\n    :else\n    (let [w (open-world! ctx spec)]\n      (if-some [refusal (:refusal w)]\n        (do (close-world! w)\n            {:refusal refusal})\n        (let [result (atom w)]\n          (try\n            (let [[w report] (reduce (fn [[w report] op]\n                                       (let [[w additions] (run-op ctx w op)]\n                                         (reset! result w)\n                                         [w (merge-report report additions)]))\n                                     [w {}]\n                                     (:ops spec))]\n              (reset! result w)\n              (assoc report :final (snapshot ctx w)))\n            (finally\n              (when-not (dead? ctx)\n                (close-world! @result)))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Inspection: the durable state after every life, read without mutating it\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn inspect\n  \"Read the durable state under `root` without mutating it: the\n   authority's projection through `authority/open!` (no reclaim, unlike\n   the grantor's reopen), the enrolled `targets`' committed values, the\n   outcome projection, each holder's progress and reply journal, and the\n   side log.\"\n  [{:keys [root holders targets]}]\n  (let [p (paths root)\n        backend (::file-journal/backend (file-journal/backend! (:authority p)))\n        opened (if backend (authority/open! backend nil) {:yin.k/status :backend-refused})\n        a (::authority/authority opened)\n        open-journal (fn [dir]\n                       (let [b (open-file-backend! dir)\n                             j (:dao.stream/handle (journal/open! b nil))]\n                         [b j]))\n        read-dir (fn [dir]\n                   (let [[b j] (open-journal dir)]\n                     (try (->data (journal-values j))\n                          (finally (file-journal/close! b)))))]\n    (try\n      {:status (:yin.k/status opened)\n       :projection (->data (when a (authority/projection a)))\n       :targets (into {}\n                      (map (fn [i]\n                             [(->data i) (if-some [r (when a (authority/target-reader a i))]\n                                           (->data (read-values r))\n                                           :absent)]))\n                      targets)\n       :outcomes (if a (->data (read-values (admission/outcome-reader a))) [])\n       :journals (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (read-dir (str (:journals p) \"/\" h \"-progress\"))]))\n                       holders)\n       :replies (into {} (map (fn [h] [h (read-dir (str (:journals p) \"/\" h \"-reply\"))]))\n                      holders)\n       :side (read-dir (:side p))}\n      (finally\n        (when a (authority/close! a))\n        (when backend (file-journal/close! backend))))))\n","numLines":1411,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1411}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P4VgMewCPUZ6xoWvvqwree","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
