{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RkwHp3hf9g2i74io29M6Fa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-support\n2\t  \"Test support for the row carrier under custody (phase 7a): real\n3\t   semantic-register machines the engine parks, the composition's source\n4\t   index, a deterministic exporter, the custody header parts and `lift`,\n5\t   rows/lift-task over one machine. It mirrors yin.vm.ucf.lift-support,\n6\t   whose AST helpers, one-slot streams, exporter and header parts it\n7\t   reuses, over yin.vm.semantic-register instead of the old kernel.\n8\t\n9\t   Every pack the 7a tests and the rows checkpoint fixtures check comes\n10\t   out of `lift`, never from a hand-built map. The one thing set by hand\n11\t   is an operation id on a wait entry (`with-op-id`), as in lift-support.\n12\t   The streams carry no random identity and `serve-table` answers s0, s1\n13\t   ... in first-asked order, so a pack's bytes are the same on every run\n14\t   and host.\"\n15\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n16\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n17\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n18\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n19\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n20\t            [yin.vm.ledger :as ledger]\n21\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n22\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n23\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n24\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n25\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n26\t            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as ls]\n27\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n28\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n29\t\n30\t\n31\t;; =============================================================================\n32\t;; The composition: code by A and the source index\n33\t;; =============================================================================\n34\t\n35\t(def source-index\n36\t  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (continuation §6.1): every vector\n37\t   `project` makes is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n38\t  (atom {}))\n39\t\n40\t\n41\t(defn project\n42\t  [ast]\n43\t  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))]\n44\t    (swap! source-index update (jing/segment-key v) (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n45\t    v))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t(def lit ls/lit)\n49\t(def v ls/v)\n50\t(def lam ls/lam)\n51\t(def app ls/app)\n52\t(def then ls/then)\n53\t(def let1 ls/let1)\n54\t(def def! ls/def!)\n55\t(def cursor-of ls/cursor-of)\n56\t(def next-of ls/next-of)\n57\t(def one-slot-stream ls/one-slot-stream)\n58\t(def serve-table ls/serve-table)\n59\t(def with-op-id ls/with-op-id)\n60\t(def occurrence ls/occurrence)\n61\t(def predecessor ls/predecessor)\n62\t(def origin ls/origin)\n63\t(def arbitration ls/arbitration)\n64\t(def op-id ls/op-id)\n65\t(def header ls/header)\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t(defn- ring\n69\t  [capacity]\n70\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n71\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t(defn- make-det-stream\n75\t  []\n76\t  (let [n (atom 0)]\n77\t    (fn [_capacity]\n78\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n79\t       :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"made-\" (swap! n inc)))})))\n80\t\n81\t\n82\t(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t(defn new-machine\n86\t  ([] (new-machine {}))\n87\t  ([opts]\n88\t   (sr/create-vm (merge {:make-stream (make-det-stream)\n89\t                         :capability-secret tu/secret\n90\t                         :modules stream-modules\n91\t                         :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))}\n92\t                        opts))))\n93\t\n94\t\n95\t(defn load-ast\n96\t  [machine ast]\n97\t  (sr/load-vector machine (project ast) code/contract))\n98\t\n99\t\n100\t;; =============================================================================\n101\t;; Machines\n102\t;; =============================================================================\n103\t\n104\t(defn parked-reader\n105\t  \"Parked on the second read of the stream it makes, A consumed: one :next\n106\t   wait over one cursor cell.\"\n107\t  []\n108\t  (let [m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n109\t                             (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n110\t                                   (let1 'c (cursor-of (v 's))\n111\t                                         (then (next-of (v 'c)) (next-of (v 'c)))))))\n112\t        src (get (:resources m0) (:stream-id (first (:wait-set m0))))]\n113\t    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n114\t    (vm/run m0)))\n115\t\n116\t\n117\t(defn parked-writer\n118\t  \"Parked on a blocked write: the warm one-slot stream keeps the value\n119\t   retained. One :put wait.\"\n120\t  []\n121\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n122\t    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n123\t    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine) {:type :stream/put :target (v 'w) :val (lit \"v\")})\n124\t          [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)]\n125\t      (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref})))))\n126\t\n127\t\n128\t(defn parked-explicit\n129\t  \"At an explicit park, its record's environment holding a cursor.\"\n130\t  []\n131\t  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n132\t                    (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n133\t                          (app (lam ['c] {:type :vm/park}) (cursor-of (v 's)))))))\n134\t\n135\t\n136\t(defn parked-linker\n137\t  \"Parked on a link request under the :running gate, so the entry carries\n138\t   no :cursor: the lift refuses it (:link-cursor-not-installed).\"\n139\t  []\n140\t  (vm/run (-> (new-machine {:link-request (ring 8) :link-response (ring 8)})\n141\t              (load-ast (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)))\n142\t              (assoc :yin.k/gate :running))))\n143\t\n144\t\n145\t(defn linked-response\n146\t  \"A link response as the linker answers one (yin.vm.linker/link-manifest):\n147\t   the image of ast, the manifest naming its tree and its :yin.semantic/code\n148\t   derivation record, and that record, from the tree to the image's A. The\n149\t   lower checks that chain (rows/check-install!, continuation §11 Q3).\"\n150\t  [ast module-name exports]\n151\t  (let [image (project ast)\n152\t        tree (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast])\n153\t        record (ledger/derive-record tree (jing/segment-key image))]\n154\t    {:status :ok\n155\t     :image {:value image}\n156\t     :manifest {:yin.module/name module-name :yin.module/exports exports\n157\t                :yin.module/tree tree\n158\t                :yin.module/derivations {:yin.semantic/code (jing/segment-key record)}}\n159\t     :derivation record\n160\t     :obligations []}))\n161\t\n162\t\n163\t(defn module-response\n164\t  []\n165\t  (linked-response (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n166\t                         (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 's))) (def! 'f (lam [] (lit 42)))))\n167\t                   'host.mod #{'f}))\n168\t\n169\t\n170\t(defn parked-installer\n171\t  \"Parked at :install with a live child blocked on its own read.\"\n172\t  []\n173\t  (let [request (ring 64) response (ring 64)\n174\t        m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n175\t                             (then (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)) (app (v 'host.mod/f)))))\n176\t        entry (first (:wait-set m0))]\n177\t    (stream/append! response (assoc (module-response) :yin.link/id (:link-id entry)))\n178\t    (vm/run m0)))\n179\t\n180\t\n181\t(defn halted-machine\n182\t  \"Halted with result 42.\"\n183\t  []\n184\t  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lit 42))))\n185\t\n186\t\n187\t(defn- fresh-cursors\n188\t  [machine]\n189\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"k1\") x (one-slot-stream \"k2\")\n190\t        [wa m1] (engine/attach-resource machine w)\n191\t        [xa m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 x)\n192\t        [c1 m3] (engine/handle-cursor m2 {:stream wa} :k1)\n193\t        [c2 m4] (engine/handle-cursor m3 {:stream xa} :k2)]\n194\t    {:c1 c1 :c2 c2 :machine m4}))\n195\t\n196\t\n197\t(defn halted-with-cursors\n198\t  \"Halted with result (f c1 c2) over two fresh cursor references nothing\n199\t   else reaches.\"\n200\t  [f]\n201\t  (let [{:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors (halted-machine))]\n202\t    (assoc machine :value (f c1 c2))))\n203\t\n204\t\n205\t(defn parked-module-store-cursors\n206\t  \"At an explicit park whose host.mod module store holds two cursor\n207\t   references, named by a module closure in the task store.\"\n208\t  []\n209\t  (let [ast (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park}) (lit 1))\n210\t        vec* (project ast)\n211\t        m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) ast))\n212\t        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n213\t        closure (first (filter #(= :closure (first %)) vec*))\n214\t        clo (values/closure (:owner machine)\n215\t                            {:type :closure :params (nth closure 2) :entry (nth closure 3)\n216\t                             :segment (get (:code-aliases machine) (jing/segment-key vec*))\n217\t                             :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n218\t    (assoc machine :store {'mod clo} :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1 'd c2}})))\n219\t\n220\t\n221\t;; =============================================================================\n222\t;; The lift, the lower's attacher\n223\t;; =============================================================================\n224\t\n225\t(defn lift-opts\n226\t  ([] (lift-opts nil))\n227\t  ([header]\n228\t   (cond-> {:source-index @source-index}\n229\t     (some? header) (assoc :header header))))\n230\t\n231\t\n232\t(defn lift\n233\t  \"rows/lift-task of machine under header (nil: the fork) with a fresh\n234\t   deterministic exporter: the pack, or the refusal's ex-data.\"\n235\t  [machine header]\n236\t  (try (rows/lift-task machine (serve-table) (lift-opts header))\n237\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n238\t         (or (ex-data e) (throw e)))))\n239\t\n240\t\n241\t(defn attacher\n242\t  \"A receiver's attach!: a fresh one-slot stream per descriptor, counting\n243\t   attaches in the atom it answers beside.\"\n244\t  []\n245\t  (let [n (atom 0)]\n246\t    {:count n\n247\t     :attach! (fn [d]\n248\t                (swap! n inc)\n249\t                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n250\t                 :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"attached-\" (:dao.stream/identity d)))})}))\n251\t\n252\t\n253\t(defn receiver\n254\t  ([] (receiver {}))\n255\t  ([opts] (new-machine opts)))\n256\t\n257\t\n258\t(defn parked-writer-shared\n259\t  \"A real machine parked on a write whose one stream handle is held\n260\t   under two resource ids: the write's own target and the environment's\n261\t   second reference.  Prepare must ask `serve!` once and key the answer\n262\t   under both.\"\n263\t  []\n264\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n265\t    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n266\t    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n267\t                       (let1 'again (v 'w2)\n268\t                             {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w)\n269\t                              :val (lit \"v\")}))\n270\t          [ra m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n271\t          [rb m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 w)]\n272\t      (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'w ra 'w2 rb})))))\n273\t\n274\t\n275\t(defn parked-writer-shared-late\n276\t  \"A real machine parked on a write whose one stream handle is held\n277\t   under two resource ids, with a third, independent stream reached\n278\t   between them -- the environment's bindings put the first alias, the\n279\t   independent stream, then the pending's alias -- so a prepare that\n280\t   serves the first alias and refuses the third leaves the second alias\n281\t   unserved, and the retry must resolve it from the record without\n282\t   serving the handle again.\"\n283\t  []\n284\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")\n285\t        x (one-slot-stream \"x\")]\n286\t    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n287\t    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n288\t                       (let1 'again (v 'w2)\n289\t                             (let1 'later-than-again (v 'x2)\n290\t                                   {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w),\n291\t                                    :val (lit \"v\")})))\n292\t          [ra m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n293\t          [rb m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 w)\n294\t          [rx m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 x)]\n295\t      (vm/run (assoc m3 :store {'w ra, 'w2 rb, 'x2 rx})))))\n296\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e817baf-a368-4767-b2d4-2b25a4b937e7","uuid":"79c8dfaf-2d27-41f9-b10f-b660a6e3f4ff","timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:46:34.473Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-support\n  \"Test support for the row carrier under custody (phase 7a): real\n   semantic-register machines the engine parks, the composition's source\n   index, a deterministic exporter, the custody header parts and `lift`,\n   rows/lift-task over one machine. It mirrors yin.vm.ucf.lift-support,\n   whose AST helpers, one-slot streams, exporter and header parts it\n   reuses, over yin.vm.semantic-register instead of the old kernel.\n\n   Every pack the 7a tests and the rows checkpoint fixtures check comes\n   out of `lift`, never from a hand-built map. The one thing set by hand\n   is an operation id on a wait entry (`with-op-id`), as in lift-support.\n   The streams carry no random identity and `serve-table` answers s0, s1\n   ... in first-asked order, so a pack's bytes are the same on every run\n   and host.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ledger :as ledger]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as ls]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A and the source index\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (continuation §6.1): every vector\n   `project` makes is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(defn project\n  [ast]\n  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))]\n    (swap! source-index update (jing/segment-key v) (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n    v))\n\n\n(def lit ls/lit)\n(def v ls/v)\n(def lam ls/lam)\n(def app ls/app)\n(def then ls/then)\n(def let1 ls/let1)\n(def def! ls/def!)\n(def cursor-of ls/cursor-of)\n(def next-of ls/next-of)\n(def one-slot-stream ls/one-slot-stream)\n(def serve-table ls/serve-table)\n(def with-op-id ls/with-op-id)\n(def occurrence ls/occurrence)\n(def predecessor ls/predecessor)\n(def origin ls/origin)\n(def arbitration ls/arbitration)\n(def op-id ls/op-id)\n(def header ls/header)\n\n\n(defn- ring\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n\n\n(defn- make-det-stream\n  []\n  (let [n (atom 0)]\n    (fn [_capacity]\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n       :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"made-\" (swap! n inc)))})))\n\n\n(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n\n\n(defn new-machine\n  ([] (new-machine {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (sr/create-vm (merge {:make-stream (make-det-stream)\n                         :capability-secret tu/secret\n                         :modules stream-modules\n                         :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))}\n                        opts))))\n\n\n(defn load-ast\n  [machine ast]\n  (sr/load-vector machine (project ast) code/contract))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Machines\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn parked-reader\n  \"Parked on the second read of the stream it makes, A consumed: one :next\n   wait over one cursor cell.\"\n  []\n  (let [m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                             (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                                   (let1 'c (cursor-of (v 's))\n                                         (then (next-of (v 'c)) (next-of (v 'c)))))))\n        src (get (:resources m0) (:stream-id (first (:wait-set m0))))]\n    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n    (vm/run m0)))\n\n\n(defn parked-writer\n  \"Parked on a blocked write: the warm one-slot stream keeps the value\n   retained. One :put wait.\"\n  []\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine) {:type :stream/put :target (v 'w) :val (lit \"v\")})\n          [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)]\n      (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref})))))\n\n\n(defn parked-explicit\n  \"At an explicit park, its record's environment holding a cursor.\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                    (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                          (app (lam ['c] {:type :vm/park}) (cursor-of (v 's)))))))\n\n\n(defn parked-linker\n  \"Parked on a link request under the :running gate, so the entry carries\n   no :cursor: the lift refuses it (:link-cursor-not-installed).\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (-> (new-machine {:link-request (ring 8) :link-response (ring 8)})\n              (load-ast (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)))\n              (assoc :yin.k/gate :running))))\n\n\n(defn linked-response\n  \"A link response as the linker answers one (yin.vm.linker/link-manifest):\n   the image of ast, the manifest naming its tree and its :yin.semantic/code\n   derivation record, and that record, from the tree to the image's A. The\n   lower checks that chain (rows/check-install!, continuation §11 Q3).\"\n  [ast module-name exports]\n  (let [image (project ast)\n        tree (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast])\n        record (ledger/derive-record tree (jing/segment-key image))]\n    {:status :ok\n     :image {:value image}\n     :manifest {:yin.module/name module-name :yin.module/exports exports\n                :yin.module/tree tree\n                :yin.module/derivations {:yin.semantic/code (jing/segment-key record)}}\n     :derivation record\n     :obligations []}))\n\n\n(defn module-response\n  []\n  (linked-response (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                         (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 's))) (def! 'f (lam [] (lit 42)))))\n                   'host.mod #{'f}))\n\n\n(defn parked-installer\n  \"Parked at :install with a live child blocked on its own read.\"\n  []\n  (let [request (ring 64) response (ring 64)\n        m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n                             (then (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)) (app (v 'host.mod/f)))))\n        entry (first (:wait-set m0))]\n    (stream/append! response (assoc (module-response) :yin.link/id (:link-id entry)))\n    (vm/run m0)))\n\n\n(defn halted-machine\n  \"Halted with result 42.\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lit 42))))\n\n\n(defn- fresh-cursors\n  [machine]\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"k1\") x (one-slot-stream \"k2\")\n        [wa m1] (engine/attach-resource machine w)\n        [xa m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 x)\n        [c1 m3] (engine/handle-cursor m2 {:stream wa} :k1)\n        [c2 m4] (engine/handle-cursor m3 {:stream xa} :k2)]\n    {:c1 c1 :c2 c2 :machine m4}))\n\n\n(defn halted-with-cursors\n  \"Halted with result (f c1 c2) over two fresh cursor references nothing\n   else reaches.\"\n  [f]\n  (let [{:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors (halted-machine))]\n    (assoc machine :value (f c1 c2))))\n\n\n(defn parked-module-store-cursors\n  \"At an explicit park whose host.mod module store holds two cursor\n   references, named by a module closure in the task store.\"\n  []\n  (let [ast (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park}) (lit 1))\n        vec* (project ast)\n        m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) ast))\n        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n        closure (first (filter #(= :closure (first %)) vec*))\n        clo (values/closure (:owner machine)\n                            {:type :closure :params (nth closure 2) :entry (nth closure 3)\n                             :segment (get (:code-aliases machine) (jing/segment-key vec*))\n                             :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n    (assoc machine :store {'mod clo} :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1 'd c2}})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The lift, the lower's attacher\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn lift-opts\n  ([] (lift-opts nil))\n  ([header]\n   (cond-> {:source-index @source-index}\n     (some? header) (assoc :header header))))\n\n\n(defn lift\n  \"rows/lift-task of machine under header (nil: the fork) with a fresh\n   deterministic exporter: the pack, or the refusal's ex-data.\"\n  [machine header]\n  (try (rows/lift-task machine (serve-table) (lift-opts header))\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n         (or (ex-data e) (throw e)))))\n\n\n(defn attacher\n  \"A receiver's attach!: a fresh one-slot stream per descriptor, counting\n   attaches in the atom it answers beside.\"\n  []\n  (let [n (atom 0)]\n    {:count n\n     :attach! (fn [d]\n                (swap! n inc)\n                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n                 :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"attached-\" (:dao.stream/identity d)))})}))\n\n\n(defn receiver\n  ([] (receiver {}))\n  ([opts] (new-machine opts)))\n\n\n(defn parked-writer-shared\n  \"A real machine parked on a write whose one stream handle is held\n   under two resource ids: the write's own target and the environment's\n   second reference.  Prepare must ask `serve!` once and key the answer\n   under both.\"\n  []\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n                       (let1 'again (v 'w2)\n                             {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w)\n                              :val (lit \"v\")}))\n          [ra m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n          [rb m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 w)]\n      (vm/run (assoc m2 :store {'w ra 'w2 rb})))))\n\n\n(defn parked-writer-shared-late\n  \"A real machine parked on a write whose one stream handle is held\n   under two resource ids, with a third, independent stream reached\n   between them -- the environment's bindings put the first alias, the\n   independent stream, then the pending's alias -- so a prepare that\n   serves the first alias and refuses the third leaves the second alias\n   unserved, and the retry must resolve it from the record without\n   serving the handle again.\"\n  []\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")\n        x (one-slot-stream \"x\")]\n    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine)\n                       (let1 'again (v 'w2)\n                             (let1 'later-than-again (v 'x2)\n                                   {:type :stream/put, :target (v 'w),\n                                    :val (lit \"v\")})))\n          [ra m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n          [rb m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 w)\n          [rx m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 x)]\n      (vm/run (assoc m3 :store {'w ra, 'w2 rb, 'x2 rx})))))\n","numLines":296,"startLine":1,"totalLines":296}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RkwHp3hf9g2i74io29M6Fa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
