{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U3JXRDGSceg7VhqF1xWTxr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer\n2\t  \"M-next stage E's peer: one life of a crash/partition scenario\n3\t   (yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-world) run as its own operating-system process,\n4\t   the process transport of linker-dht 14.1.3 for the JVM and Node.\n5\t\n6\t   The parent (yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-process-test) writes the life's spec\n7\t   as EDN to a file and starts this program with that path.  Every event\n8\t   the life emits is printed at once as one line, `E|` followed by the\n9\t   event as EDN; the life's report arrives as {:event :done}.  When the\n10\t   life's cut fires the peer prints {:event :cut} and blocks forever:\n11\t   the parent destroys the process there (SIGKILL), so nothing the life\n12\t   did after its cut ever happens and nothing it did before is undone --\n13\t   the durable media hold exactly what a killed process leaves.\n14\t\n15\t   JVM: `java -cp <classpath> clojure.main -m yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer\n16\t   spec.edn`.  Node: the shadow-cljs :node-script build of `main`, which\n17\t   the parent compiles before its first Node life.\"\n18\t  (:require #?@(:cljd []\n19\t                :clj [[clojure.edn :as edn]]\n20\t                :cljs [[cljs.reader :as reader]])\n21\t            [yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-world :as world]))\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t(defn- read-spec\n25\t  [text]\n26\t  #?(:cljd nil\n27\t     :clj (edn/read-string text)\n28\t     :cljs (reader/read-string text)))\n29\t\n30\t\n31\t(defn- slurp-file\n32\t  [path]\n33\t  #?(:cljd nil\n34\t     :clj (slurp path)\n35\t     :cljs (.toString (.readFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path) \"utf8\")))\n36\t\n37\t\n38\t(defn- write-line!\n39\t  [line]\n40\t  #?(:cljd nil\n41\t     :clj (locking *out*\n42\t            (.write *out* (str line \"\\n\"))\n43\t            (.flush *out*))\n44\t     ;; synchronous: a pipe write on Node may otherwise still be queued\n45\t     ;; when the peer blocks at its cut\n46\t     :cljs (.writeSync (js/require \"fs\") 1 (str line \"\\n\"))))\n47\t\n48\t\n49\t(defn- block-forever!\n50\t  \"Never return: the parent kills the process here.\"\n51\t  []\n52\t  #?(:cljd nil\n53\t     :clj @(promise)\n54\t     :cljs (loop []\n55\t             (recur))))\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t(defn- emit!\n59\t  [event]\n60\t  (write-line! (str \"E|\" (binding [*print-namespace-maps* false\n61\t                                   *print-length* nil\n62\t                                   *print-level* nil]\n63\t                           (pr-str (world/->data event))))))\n64\t\n65\t\n66\t(defn- host\n67\t  []\n68\t  #?(:cljd :dart :clj :jvm :cljs :node))\n69\t\n70\t\n71\t(defn- pid\n72\t  []\n73\t  #?(:cljd nil\n74\t     :clj (.pid (java.lang.ProcessHandle/current))\n75\t     :cljs (.-pid js/process)))\n76\t\n77\t\n78\t(defn run-spec!\n79\t  \"Run the life whose spec is EDN `text`, printing its events.\"\n80\t  [text]\n81\t  (let [spec (read-spec text)\n82\t        ctx (world/context {:cut (:cut spec)\n83\t                            :fail (:fail spec)\n84\t                            :emit! emit!\n85\t                            :at-cut block-forever!})]\n86\t    (emit! {:event :started :host (host) :pid (pid) :cut (:cut spec)})\n87\t    (try\n88\t      (let [report (if (:inspect spec)\n89\t                     (world/inspect spec)\n90\t                     (world/run-life ctx spec))]\n91\t        (emit! {:event :done :report report}))\n92\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n93\t        (if (world/killed? e)\n94\t          (block-forever!)\n95\t          (emit! {:event :error\n96\t                  :message #?(:cljd (str e) :clj (ex-message e) :cljs (ex-message e))\n97\t                  :data (world/->data (ex-data e))}))))))\n98\t\n99\t\n100\t#?(:cljd nil\n101\t   :clj\n102\t   (defn -main\n103\t     [path]\n104\t     (run-spec! (slurp-file path))\n105\t     (shutdown-agents)\n106\t     (System/exit 0)))\n107\t\n108\t\n109\t#?(:cljd nil\n110\t   :cljs\n111\t   (defn main\n112\t     [path]\n113\t     (run-spec! (slurp-file path))))\n114\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e817baf-a368-4767-b2d4-2b25a4b937e7","uuid":"43fdccb5-e708-45a3-9c7b-8973c25b91da","timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:46:35.230Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_peer.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer\n  \"M-next stage E's peer: one life of a crash/partition scenario\n   (yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-world) run as its own operating-system process,\n   the process transport of linker-dht 14.1.3 for the JVM and Node.\n\n   The parent (yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-process-test) writes the life's spec\n   as EDN to a file and starts this program with that path.  Every event\n   the life emits is printed at once as one line, `E|` followed by the\n   event as EDN; the life's report arrives as {:event :done}.  When the\n   life's cut fires the peer prints {:event :cut} and blocks forever:\n   the parent destroys the process there (SIGKILL), so nothing the life\n   did after its cut ever happens and nothing it did before is undone --\n   the durable media hold exactly what a killed process leaves.\n\n   JVM: `java -cp <classpath> clojure.main -m yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer\n   spec.edn`.  Node: the shadow-cljs :node-script build of `main`, which\n   the parent compiles before its first Node life.\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd []\n                :clj [[clojure.edn :as edn]]\n                :cljs [[cljs.reader :as reader]])\n            [yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-world :as world]))\n\n\n(defn- read-spec\n  [text]\n  #?(:cljd nil\n     :clj (edn/read-string text)\n     :cljs (reader/read-string text)))\n\n\n(defn- slurp-file\n  [path]\n  #?(:cljd nil\n     :clj (slurp path)\n     :cljs (.toString (.readFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path) \"utf8\")))\n\n\n(defn- write-line!\n  [line]\n  #?(:cljd nil\n     :clj (locking *out*\n            (.write *out* (str line \"\\n\"))\n            (.flush *out*))\n     ;; synchronous: a pipe write on Node may otherwise still be queued\n     ;; when the peer blocks at its cut\n     :cljs (.writeSync (js/require \"fs\") 1 (str line \"\\n\"))))\n\n\n(defn- block-forever!\n  \"Never return: the parent kills the process here.\"\n  []\n  #?(:cljd nil\n     :clj @(promise)\n     :cljs (loop []\n             (recur))))\n\n\n(defn- emit!\n  [event]\n  (write-line! (str \"E|\" (binding [*print-namespace-maps* false\n                                   *print-length* nil\n                                   *print-level* nil]\n                           (pr-str (world/->data event))))))\n\n\n(defn- host\n  []\n  #?(:cljd :dart :clj :jvm :cljs :node))\n\n\n(defn- pid\n  []\n  #?(:cljd nil\n     :clj (.pid (java.lang.ProcessHandle/current))\n     :cljs (.-pid js/process)))\n\n\n(defn run-spec!\n  \"Run the life whose spec is EDN `text`, printing its events.\"\n  [text]\n  (let [spec (read-spec text)\n        ctx (world/context {:cut (:cut spec)\n                            :fail (:fail spec)\n                            :emit! emit!\n                            :at-cut block-forever!})]\n    (emit! {:event :started :host (host) :pid (pid) :cut (:cut spec)})\n    (try\n      (let [report (if (:inspect spec)\n                     (world/inspect spec)\n                     (world/run-life ctx spec))]\n        (emit! {:event :done :report report}))\n      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n        (if (world/killed? e)\n          (block-forever!)\n          (emit! {:event :error\n                  :message #?(:cljd (str e) :clj (ex-message e) :cljs (ex-message e))\n                  :data (world/->data (ex-data e))}))))))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :clj\n   (defn -main\n     [path]\n     (run-spec! (slurp-file path))\n     (shutdown-agents)\n     (System/exit 0)))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :cljs\n   (defn main\n     [path]\n     (run-spec! (slurp-file path))))\n","numLines":114,