{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AMuuYLpvmzEdbeyjjug86a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-process-test\n2\t  \"M-next stage E across real processes: every scenario of\n3\t   yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-scenarios over the ordered JVM/Node host pairs of\n4\t   linker-dht 14.1.1 -- JVM to JVM and Node to Node as the same-host\n5\t   controls, JVM to Node and Node to JVM across hosts -- each life its\n6\t   own operating-system process (yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer) over the\n7\t   scenario's durable file media, each cut a real kill: the peer prints\n8\t   the cut and blocks, and this harness destroys it forcibly (SIGKILL)\n9\t   there.  Nothing crosses between lives but the bytes on disk: the\n10\t   authority's ledger, the journals, the content store's canonical\n11\t   bodies and the side log.\n12\t\n13\t   The Node peer is required: it is compiled here, before the first\n14\t   Node life (shadow-cljs's :vm-bench node-script build with the peer as\n15\t   its main, to target/stage-e-peer.js), so this gate cannot skip; a\n16\t   failed build fails the test.  The JVM peer runs from classes this\n17\t   harness compiles ahead of time into a fresh directory, so each JVM\n18\t   life starts in seconds.\n19\t\n20\t   No port is used and none is reserved.  Real processes are polled\n21\t   with bounded deadlines; every process is destroyed in a finally.  No\n22\t   wall-clock sleep is taken: time inside the protocol advances only by\n23\t   the clock readings a life's spec appends as ticks.\n24\t\n25\t   Each scenario run appends one line to the durability record\n26\t   (target/stage-e-durability.edn): the scenario, the host pair, and for\n27\t   every life its host, pid, cut and whether it was killed.\"\n28\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n29\t            [clojure.java.io :as io]\n30\t            [clojure.java.shell :as shell]\n31\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n32\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n33\t            [yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-scenarios :as sc])\n34\t  (:import (java.util.concurrent LinkedBlockingQueue TimeUnit)))\n35\t\n36\t\n37\t(def ^:private life-ms\n38\t  \"Bound on one life, from process start to its done or cut event.\"\n39\t  180000)\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t(def pairs\n43\t  \"The ordered source/receiver host pairs this harness runs: the two\n44\t   same-host controls and both cross-host orders.\"\n45\t  [[:jvm :jvm] [:jvm :node] [:node :jvm] [:node :node]])\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t;; =============================================================================\n49\t;; The peers\n50\t;; =============================================================================\n51\t\n52\t\n53\t(def ^:private node-peer \"target/stage-e-peer.js\")\n54\t\n55\t\n56\t(def ^:private classes-dir\n57\t  (str \"target/stage-e-classes-\" (random-uuid)))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(defn- run-build!\n61\t  [what command]\n62\t  (let [{:keys [exit out err]} (apply shell/sh command)]\n63\t    (when-not (zero? exit)\n64\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"stage E: the \" what \" build failed\")\n65\t                      {:command command :exit exit :out out :err err})))))\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t(def ^:private node-built\n69\t  (delay\n70\t    (run-build! \"Node peer\"\n71\t                [\"clj\" \"-M:cljs\" \"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"compile\" \"vm-bench\"\n72\t                 \"--config-merge\"\n73\t                 (str \"{:main yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer/main :output-to \\\"\" node-peer \"\\\"}\")])\n74\t    (when-not (.exists (io/file node-peer))\n75\t      (throw (ex-info \"stage E: the Node peer build wrote nothing\" {:path node-peer})))\n76\t    true))\n77\t\n78\t\n79\t(defn- java-bin\n80\t  []\n81\t  (str (System/getProperty \"java.home\") \"/bin/java\"))\n82\t\n83\t\n84\t(def ^:private jvm-built\n85\t  (delay\n86\t    (.mkdirs (io/file classes-dir))\n87\t    (run-build! \"JVM peer classes\"\n88\t                [(java-bin) \"-cp\" (str classes-dir java.io.File/pathSeparator\n89\t                                       (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\"))\n90\t                 \"clojure.main\" \"-e\"\n91\t                 (str \"(binding [*compile-path* \\\"\" classes-dir \"\\\"]\"\n92\t                      \" (compile 'yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer))\")])\n93\t    true))\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t(defn- command\n97\t  [host spec-path]\n98\t  (case host\n99\t    :jvm (do @jvm-built\n100\t             [(java-bin) \"-cp\" (str classes-dir java.io.File/pathSeparator\n101\t                                    (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\"))\n102\t              \"clojure.main\" \"-m\" \"yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-peer\" spec-path])\n103\t    :node (do @node-built\n104\t              [\"node\" node-peer spec-path])))\n105\t\n106\t\n107\t;; =============================================================================\n108\t;; One life, one process\n109\t;; =============================================================================\n110\t\n111\t\n112\t(defn- line-pump\n113\t  \"A daemon thread that puts every stdout line of `process` on a queue,\n114\t   then ::eof.\"\n115\t  [process]\n116\t  (let [q (LinkedBlockingQueue.)\n117\t        t (Thread. ^Runnable\n118\t           (fn []\n119\t             (try\n120\t               (with-open [r (io/reader (.getInputStream process))]\n121\t                 (doseq [line (line-seq r)]\n122\t                   (.put q line)))\n123\t               (catch Throwable _ nil)\n124\t               (finally (.put q ::eof)))))]\n125\t    (.setDaemon t true)\n126\t    (.start t)\n127\t    q))\n128\t\n129\t\n130\t(defn- parse-event\n131\t  [line]\n132\t  (when (str/starts-with? line \"E|\")\n133\t    (edn/read-string (subs line 2))))\n134\t\n135\t\n136\t(defn- destroy!\n137\t  [process]\n138\t  (.destroyForcibly process)\n139\t  (.waitFor process 30 TimeUnit/SECONDS))\n140\t\n141\t\n142\t(defn run-life-in-process!\n143\t  \"Run one life of `spec` as a peer process on `host`: answer the same\n144\t   result shape as the in-