{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LdAUaiG3V3Xci8zsokUNEY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint\n2\t  \"The rows inspector of phase 7a (phase-7 plan §3.3): the custody grammar\n3\t   of a version-3 row pack, checked on its canonical bytes, and the\n4\t   operation baseline it carries. It replaces yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint at the\n5\t   authority's three call sites (grant/offer!, completion/report!,\n6\t   admission's accepted-baseline); the version-1/2 inspector stays for the\n7\t   old codec's tests until phase 8.\n8\t\n9\t   A pack has two identities. The **pack address** is the BLAKE3 segment\n10\t   address of the pack's canonical bytes: the storage key, the one a\n11\t   dao.jing content store verifies on put, and the ledger's :yin.k/id. The\n12\t   **root id** is the :task row's own content address inside the pack: the\n13\t   semantic identity of the transported state, which `emit` makes one pack\n14\t   per root on every host by sorting the rows. The baseline names the root\n15\t   id as :yin.k/root; the address is the caller's.\n16\t\n17\t   `inspect` checks, in this order, and the first to fail decides: the\n18\t   address against the bytes (:yin.k/hash-mismatch carrying the claimed\n19\t   :yin.k/address and the :yin.k/computed one), one canonical CBOR item\n20\t   (:yin.k/undecodable :bytes), the carrier itself through rows/decode\n21\t   (gate, structure, graph, every row hash, canonical form and cursor-cell\n22\t   numbering, frames: the codec's own refusal), a :task root, and then\n23\t   rows/custody-baseline: the root's custody slot by kind, every task's\n24\t   kind and role, every :install pending's row, a nil slot on every child,\n25\t   and every operation id on a :put, :ffi-request or :link-request pending\n26\t   of the root and its children against the root's occurrence, origin and\n27\t   counter, duplicates refused. A nil slot is a fork: no id may be carried\n28\t   and the baseline says :yin.k/fork true.\n29\t\n30\t   Answers the operation baseline\n31\t\n32\t     {:yin.k/kind        k\n33\t      :yin.k/root        B          ; the root id\n34\t      :yin.k/occurrence  O          ; absent on a halted root and a fork\n35\t      :yin.k/origin      {...}      ; absent on a first park and a fork\n36\t      :yin.k/arbitration {...}      ; absent on a halted root and a fork\n37\t      :yin.k/next-op-seq n          ; absent on a halted root and a fork\n38\t      :yin.k/ops         {op-id digest}\n39\t      :yin.k/fork        true}      ; a nil slot only\n40\t\n41\t   digest being the BLAKE3 hex of the canonical bytes of [:yin.k/append\n42\t   target-identity payload], the payload as the wire slot holds it.\n43\t   Every refusal is a data outcome carrying :yin.k/status; nothing here\n44\t   throws on any input but a codec defect.\"\n45\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n46\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n47\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]))\n48\t\n49\t\n50\t(defn- answer\n51\t  \"Run f, answering its value or the refusal it threw. A throw without\n52\t   the refusal vocabulary is a defect and propagates.\"\n53\t  [f]\n54\t  (try (f)\n55\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n56\t         (let [d (ex-data e)]\n57\t           (if (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d (throw e))))))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(defn- computed-address\n61\t  \"The segment address of bytes under the algorithm address names, or\n62\t   BLAKE3 when it names none; nil when bytes are not bytes.\"\n63\t  [address bytes]\n64\t  (when (cbor/byte-payload? bytes)\n65\t    (let [algo (or (:algorithm (jing/parse-segment-address address)) :blake3)]\n66\t      (keyword \"segment\" (str (get-in jing/registry [algo :address-id]) \"-\"\n67\t                              (jing/digest-bytes algo bytes))))))\n68\t\n69\t\n70\t(defn inspect-pack\n71\t  \"The operation baseline of the decoded pack wire (a map\n72\t   dao.jing.cbor/decode answered), or the first refusal as data.\"\n73\t  [wire]\n74\t  (answer\n75\t    (fn []\n76\t      (let [task (rows/decode wire)]\n77\t        (when-not (= :task (:kind task))\n78\t          (throw (ex-info \"Checkpoint refused: undecodable\"\n79\t                          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/kind :root :yin.k/path [:yin.k/root]})))\n80\t        (assoc (rows/custody-baseline task) :yin.k/root (:yin.k/root wire))))))\n81\t\n82\t\n83\t(defn inspect\n84\t  \"The operation baseline of the pack whose canonical bytes are bytes\n85\t   under the segment address address (verified under the algorithm it\n86\t   names), or the first refusal as data.\"\n87\t  [address bytes]\n88\t  (answer\n89\t    (fn []\n90\t      (when-not (and (cbor/byte-payload? bytes) (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bytes))\n91\t        (throw (ex-info \"Checkpoint refused: hash-mismatch\"\n92\t                        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/hash-mismatch\n93\t                         :yin.k/address address\n94\t                         :yin.k/computed (computed-address address bytes)})))\n95\t      (let [wire (try (cbor/decode bytes)\n96\t                      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n97\t                        (throw (ex-info \"Checkpoint refused: undecodable\"\n98\t                                        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/path []\n99\t                                         :yin.k/kind :bytes :yin.k/refusal (cbor/refusal e)}))))]\n100\t        (if (map? wire)\n101\t          (inspect-pack wire)\n102\t          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/path [] :yin.k/kind :body})))))\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e817baf-a368-4767-b2d4-2b25a4b937e7","uuid":"ee33b018-d775-4d85-8270-b41813b5f049","timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:47:02.328Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7d/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows/checkpoint.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint\n  \"The rows inspector of phase 7a (phase-7 plan §3.3): the custody grammar\n   of a version-3 row pack, checked on its canonical bytes, and the\n   operation baseline it carries. It replaces yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint at the\n   authority's three call sites (grant/offer!, completion/report!,\n   admission's accepted-baseline); the version-1/2 inspector stays for the\n   old codec's tests until phase 8.\n\n   A pack has two identities. The **pack address** is the BLAKE3 segment\n   address of the pack's canonical bytes: the storage key, the one a\n   dao.jing content store verifies on put, and the ledger's :yin.k/id. The\n   **root id** is the :task row's own content address inside the pack: the\n   semantic identity of the transported state, which `emit` makes one pack\n   per root on every host by sorting the rows. The baseline names the root\n   id as :yin.k/root; the address is the caller's.\n\n   `inspect` checks, in this order, and the first to fail decides: the\n   address against the bytes (:yin.k/hash-mismatch carrying the claimed\n   :yin.k/address and the :yin.k/computed one), one canonical CBOR item\n   (:yin.k/undecodable :bytes), the carrier itself through rows/decode\n   (gate, structure, graph, every row hash, canonical form and cursor-cell\n   numbering, frames: the codec's own refusal), a :task root, and then\n   rows/custody-baseline: the root's custody slot by kind, every task's\n   kind and role, every :install pending's row, a nil slot on every child,\n   and every operation id on a :put, :ffi-request or :link-request pending\n   of the root and its children against the root's occurrence, origin and\n   counter, duplicates refused. A nil slot is a fork: no id may be carried\n   and the baseline says :yin.k/fork true.\n\n   Answers the operation baseline\n\n     {:yin.k/kind        k\n      :yin.k/root        B          ; the root id\n      :yin.k/occurrence  O          ; absent on a halted root and a fork\n      :yin.k/origin      {...}      ; absent on a first park and a fork\n      :yin.k/arbitration {...}      ; absent on a halted root and a fork\n      :yin.k/next-op-seq n          ; absent on a halted root and a fork\n      :yin.k/ops         {op-id digest}\n      :yin.k/fork        true}      ; a nil slot only\n\n   digest being the BLAKE3 hex of the canonical bytes of [:yin.k/append\n   target-identity payload], the payload as the wire slot holds it.\n   Every refusal is a data outcome carrying :yin.k/status; nothing here\n   throws on any input but a codec defect.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]))\n\n\n(defn- answer\n  \"Run f, answering its value or the refusal it threw. A throw without\n   the refusal vocabulary is a defect and propagates.\"\n  [f]\n  (try (f)\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n         (let [d (ex-data e)]\n           (if (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn- computed-address\n  \"The segment address of bytes under the algorithm address names, or\n   BLAKE3 when it names none; nil when bytes are not bytes.\"\n  [address bytes]\n  (when (cbor/byte-payload? bytes)\n    (let [algo (or (:algorithm (jing/parse-segment-address address)) :blake3)]\n      (keyword \"segment\" (str (get-in jing/registry [algo :address-id]) \"-\"\n                              (jing/digest-bytes algo bytes))))))\n\n\n(defn inspect-pack\n  \"The operation baseline of the decoded pack wire (a map\n   dao.jing.cbor/decode answered), or the first refusal as data.\"\n  [wire]\n  (answer\n    (fn []\n      (let [task (rows/decode wire)]\n        (when-not (= :task (:kind task))\n          (throw (ex-info \"Checkpoint refused: undecodable\"\n                          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/kind :root :yin.k/path [:yin.k/root]})))\n        (assoc (rows/custody-baseline task) :yin.k/root (:yin.k/root wire))))))\n\n\n(defn inspect\n  \"The operation baseline of the pack whose canonical bytes are bytes\n   under the segment address address (verified under the algorithm it\n   names), or the first refusal as data.\"\n  [address bytes]\n  (answer\n    (fn []\n      (when-not (and (cbor/byte-payload? bytes) (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bytes))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Checkpoint refused: hash-mismatch\"\n                        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/hash-mismatch\n                         :yin.k/address address\n                         :yin.k/computed (computed-address address bytes)})))\n      (let [wire (try (cbor/decode bytes)\n                      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                        (throw (ex-info \"Checkpoint refused: undecodable\"\n                                        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/path []\n                                         :yin.k/kind :bytes :yin.k/refusal (cbor/refusal e)}))))]\n        (if (map? wire)\n          (inspect-pack wire)\n          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/path [] :yin.k/kind :body})))))\n","numLines":103,"startLine":1,"totalLines":103}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LdAUaiG3V3Xci8zsokUNEY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
